        backlog:RS_FlowPointsRecorded ,
        backlog:RS_ImpedimentNamesWhatItBlocks ,
        backlog:RS_ObligationsFollowStatus ,
        backlog:RS_PlanBeforeStart ,
        backlog:RS_ReadinessChecked ,
        backlog:RS_RepairReprioritises ,
        backlog:RS_ReviewNeedsControlRun ,
        backlog:RS_StatusHistoryRecorded .
ex:Mission_Midterm a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "A SEN0401 student sits a midterm exam on chapters 1 to 8, built from the course's own verified material"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "The SEN0401 midterm exam covers chapters 1 to 8 of Mastering Bitcoin's third edition as the course teaches them. Two exams are built, for a physical printed paper, from ONE general exam engine that makes cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect questions (today's engines are chapter specific). The question types and styles suit a printed paper; the critical points the owner explained in the course are revived from the slides, speaker notes, corpus and stories; methods reduce the printed pages and the mistakes in giving answers; and a reliable method reads, assesses and grades each student's paper. Items need course knowledge and are mostly at the higher Bloom levels; multiple-choice answer letters are evenly distributed and fill-in option banks are randomised; the paper is print-safe, white and line-based, with light themes; no term is fabricated; no student's personal data is used (synthetic stand-ins may be); versions are incremented." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner direction of Wednesday 2026-10-28 14:21 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator: the midterm is built after the current chapters are completed and is held next week; the owner's answers: coverage chapters 1 to 8; delivery without a stated preference (default printed paper plus answer key, with CATS/QTI export); Exam Studio conventions (multiple-choice letters evenly distributed, fill-in option banks randomised, print-safe, no fabricated terms, items need course knowledge, higher Bloom levels in the majority). VERIFIED GAP it is set from: the assessment ontology 04-assessment/sen0401_assessment_v1_0_0.ttl holds the Midterm component (30 percent) and states that no exam items are held yet; nothing else of the exam exists. MATURED 2026-10-29: OWNER'S WORDS of 2026-10-29 (Thursday 2026-10-29 15:08 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator): the owner starts the midterm mission now. Mission input: use the interactive HTML pages' exam engine to build TWO exams for SEN0401; today's engines are chapter specific, so build a general engine for cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect questions; restrict question types and styles to those that suit a physical printed paper; revive the critical points he explained in the course (take them from the slides, speaker notes, corpus and stories; list plainly what could not be found, so that he is asked); methods to reduce printed pages; methods to reduce mistakes in giving answers; a reliable method to read, assess and grade each student's paper. Existing exam conventions: multiple-choice answer letters evenly distributed, fill-in option banks randomised, print-safe white and line-based, no fabricated terms, items need course knowledge, Bloom majority higher-order, versions incremented, light themes, no personal data of students (synthetic stand-ins allowed). Chapters 1 to 8, physical paper, midterm next week; the budget is this week's usage limit. The mission is set from verified gaps only: first analyse what exists and say the gaps openly. VERIFIED GAPS (measured 2026-10-29 by the lineage agent on the repository as it stands): (G1) the exam engines are chapter specific: each of the 8 pages carries its own exam mode (screen based, started with a release code) over its own bank; no item belongs to more than one chapter (the bank field concept names one concept) and no engine builds an exam across chapters. (G2) the 8 banks hold 1,453 items, ALL single-answer four-option multiple choice (no fill-in, matching, ordering, calculation or written item); the levels are Remember 322, Understand 413, Apply 483, Analyze 235; Apply and Analyze together are 49.4 percent, Analyze alone 16.2 percent; chapter 8 holds 127 items, all Remember; chapter 6 has no Analyze item and chapter 7 has two; the answer letters are even except chapter 8 (30, 41, 25, 31); the correct option is the longest in 31.6 percent of items (chance is 25). (G3) nothing prints an exam: the pages' print styles only hide the interface; there is no paper layout, no two-version builder, no page-reduction method, no answer sheet. (G4) nothing reads or grades a paper: no scanning, reading, key matching or grading tool exists in the repository; the Exam Studio toolset (renderer, 19 quality gates, grading pipeline, CATS export) is NOT in this repository. (G5) the critical points the owner explained are not recorded as such anywhere: no slide, note or bank item carries such a mark. (G6) cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect items do not exist (0 of 1,453). (G7) nothing in the repository tests an item for fabricated terms or for needing course knowledge; the bank check tool covers the structure of the banks only. The earlier statement (queued 2026-10-28, committed in v0.576.0) named a printed paper with answer key AND a CATS/QTI export and one exam; the owner's words of 2026-10-29 replace those clauses (physical printed paper, two exams); the Mission output was never closed at a commit (closedAtCommit PENDING), so the mission matures here before it closes." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_Abandoned ;
    backlog:outcomeRationale "Cancelled on 2026-10-29. The owner answered the route question: the exam scope is covered by amending the mission of the course and updating its lineage, not by a separate lineage, and he corrected the chapter scope. The fourth lineage was advanced to LS_Backlogged before that answer (a disclosed slip; see ex:IA3_ExamMission). Its exam chain is re-admitted in the third lineage under ex:Mission_V2. The mission ex:Mission_Midterm is kept as history. The outcome statement it carried before: The instructor holds two exams for chapters 1 to 8, each as a print-ready paper with its answer key, made by one general engine, together with a method and a tool that read, assess and grade a student's paper, before the midterm of next week." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out4_Mission ;
    backlog:missionSource "The owner's direction quoted above; the verified gaps of chapters 1 to 8 are the change requests ex:CR3_Ch01DeckCheck and ex:CR3_Ch05DeckCheck and the pending ex:CR3_GateArcDark, ex:CR3_DeckCh06Slide51 (they come first)." .
ex:Out4_Mission a backlog:StageOutput ;
    rdfs:label "Closure of the Mission stage of the fourth lineage"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage4 ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Mission ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "ab805ae5d8131f1bdf69ad9732759fdb586bef1926678f1bc51a702f1e158790" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "9f8d8dc" .
