ex:Scope4 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Two printed exams for chapters 1 to 8 from one general engine, with the critical points, the paper rules and a reliable grading method"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage4 ; backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission_Midterm ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: (1) the critical points of chapters 1 to 8 listed with their sources, and the points not found listed for the owner; (2) one general exam engine, as new tool files, that builds an exam across chapters; (3) the items of TWO exams, grounded in sources, in question types that suit a physical printed paper; (4) the paper rules (types, styles, page reduction) as SHACL; (5) the two exams as print-ready papers with answer keys and an answer sheet that reduces mistakes; (6) a reliable method and tool to read, assess and grade a student's paper, shown on synthetic papers. OUT: screen delivery and CATS/QTI export, any change to the pages, chapters 9 to 14, real student data, and the owner's own decisions (put to him, never taken). OWNER'S WORDS of 2026-10-29 (Thursday 2026-10-29 15:08 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator): the owner starts the midterm mission now. Mission input: use the interactive HTML pages' exam engine to build TWO exams for SEN0401; today's engines are chapter specific, so build a general engine for cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect questions; restrict question types and styles to those that suit a physical printed paper; revive the critical points he explained in the course (take them from the slides, speaker notes, corpus and stories; list plainly what could not be found, so that he is asked); methods to reduce printed pages; methods to reduce mistakes in giving answers; a reliable method to read, assess and grade each student's paper. Existing exam conventions: multiple-choice answer letters evenly distributed, fill-in option banks randomised, print-safe white and line-based, no fabricated terms, items need course knowledge, Bloom majority higher-order, versions incremented, light themes, no personal data of students (synthetic stand-ins allowed). Chapters 1 to 8, physical paper, midterm next week; the budget is this week's usage limit. The mission is set from verified gaps only: first analyse what exists and say the gaps openly. VERIFIED GAPS (measured 2026-10-29 by the lineage agent on the repository as it stands): (G1) the exam engines are chapter specific: each of the 8 pages carries its own exam mode (screen based, started with a release code) over its own bank; no item belongs to more than one chapter (the bank field concept names one concept) and no engine builds an exam across chapters. (G2) the 8 banks hold 1,453 items, ALL single-answer four-option multiple choice (no fill-in, matching, ordering, calculation or written item); the levels are Remember 322, Understand 413, Apply 483, Analyze 235; Apply and Analyze together are 49.4 percent, Analyze alone 16.2 percent; chapter 8 holds 127 items, all Remember; chapter 6 has no Analyze item and chapter 7 has two; the answer letters are even except chapter 8 (30, 41, 25, 31); the correct option is the longest in 31.6 percent of items (chance is 25). (G3) nothing prints an exam: the pages' print styles only hide the interface; there is no paper layout, no two-version builder, no page-reduction method, no answer sheet. (G4) nothing reads or grades a paper: no scanning, reading, key matching or grading tool exists in the repository; the Exam Studio toolset (renderer, 19 quality gates, grading pipeline, CATS export) is NOT in this repository. (G5) the critical points the owner explained are not recorded as such anywhere: no slide, note or bank item carries such a mark. (G6) cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect items do not exist (0 of 1,453). (G7) nothing in the repository tests an item for fabricated terms or for needing course knowledge; the bank check tool covers the structure of the banks only." ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area4_Sources, ex:Area4_Exams, ex:Area4_Paper, ex:Area4_Grading ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl4_NoDelivery, ex:Excl4_LaterChapters, ex:Excl4_StudentData, ex:Excl4_OwnerDecisions ;
    backlog:producedByStage ex:Out4_Scope ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable ex:Del4_CriticalPoints, ex:Del4_Engine, ex:Del4_Items, ex:Del4_PaperRules, ex:Del4_Papers, ex:Del4_Grading .
