ex:CR3_ExamMission a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The course also assesses what it teaches: two printed exams (midterm and make-up) for the chapters the instructor fixes, from one general engine, with a reliable grading method"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_ExamMission, ex:Mission_V2 ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's words, Thursday 2026-10-29, the owner's words relayed by the coordinator (mission input 15:08 Istanbul; the owner's correction of the chapter scope and of the route the same day). MISSION INPUT: OWNER'S WORDS of 2026-10-29 (Thursday 2026-10-29 15:08 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator): the owner starts the midterm mission now. Mission input: use the interactive HTML pages' exam engine to build TWO exams for SEN0401; today's engines are chapter specific, so build a general engine for cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect questions; restrict question types and styles to those that suit a physical printed paper; revive the critical points he explained in the course (take them from the slides, speaker notes, corpus and stories; list plainly what could not be found, so that he is asked); methods to reduce printed pages; methods to reduce mistakes in giving answers; a reliable method to read, assess and grade each student's paper. Existing exam conventions: multiple-choice answer letters evenly distributed, fill-in option banks randomised, print-safe white and line-based, no fabricated terms, items need course knowledge, Bloom majority higher-order, versions incremented, light themes, no personal data of students (synthetic stand-ins allowed). Physical paper; the midterm is next week; the budget is this week's usage limit. The mission is set from verified gaps only: first analyse what exists and say the gaps openly. THE OWNER'S ANSWER ON THE ROUTE: does the mission and scope match the exam scope? If so, updating the lineage and the prioritisation of the exam is enough; otherwise the mission can be enhanced to cover the exam work and the lineage updated. No separate lineage and no pre-chain urgent item unless the rulings leave no other way. MEASURED: the mission of the third lineage (ex:Mission) and its scope (ex:Scope3) say nothing about an exam: the scope's IN list is the link passes and the carried open work, and its OUT list does not name an exam; the exam work therefore does not match the mission as stated, so the mission was not set for it. The routing test (G104, narrative item 4) gives route (c): a mission-statement change, the same lineage under a better statement, decided by the owner. THE OWNER'S STATEMENTS ABOUT THE CHAPTERS (recorded here, not in the mission text): the owner's own words: The exact chapter content will be cleared tomorrow after the completion of the lectures. For SEN0401, we will be able to cover chapter 6 and all other chapters are in the scope of the exam. Possibly, we will not be able to finish Chapter 7. The coordinator's reading of that word (a reading, not the owner's text): the chapter list is NOT fixed to chapters 1 to 8; chapters 1 to 6 are in the exam scope; chapter 7 is doubtful; the final list is due 2026-10-30, after the lectures. The lineage agent builds every chapter-specific item against a chapter list that is a PARAMETER of the engine, fixed by the instructor before each sitting. THE EXAMS: two, the midterm and a make-up exam over the same chapters, each a 60-minute sitting on physical printed paper. THE TIME BOX: chapter work restarts on Sunday 2026-11-01, after the weekly usage limit resets; until then only the exam scope is worked; when it restarts, the pages of chapters 1 to 6 are measured and completed first, chapters 7 and 8 only if time remains; chapter 11 and chapters 9 and above stay paused (nothing of them is started, so no urgent interruption is declared)." .
ex:IA3_ExamMission a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What amending the mission and moving the exam chain into the third lineage costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ExamMission ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3, ex:Lineage4 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "AFFECTED: the mission (a NEW statement ex:Mission_V2 that supersedes ex:Mission; ex:Mission stays as history and stays the mission the third lineage's recorded Mission output was computed for); the third lineage's Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages (a revision from the Scope stage, G127: four outputs retracted and rebuilt, the Mission output stays); the fourth lineage (set down: as-is assessment, closure report marked cancelled, status Abandoned). NOT AFFECTED: every Done item, the executors, the decks and pages, every committed file, the evidence. MEASURED BEFORE THE ROUTE WAS CHOSEN: the mission digest of the third lineage changes when the new mission belongs to the lineage or when the lineage's mission pointer moves (0d854051ea52ba05 becomes 52f0291f178728b1) and stays when ex:Mission_V2 is a free-standing superseding statement; a revision from the Mission stage is refused by the framework (StageRevisionShape: rebuilding from the mission is a LineageRestart). The route therefore keeps ex:Lineage3 pointing at ex:Mission, and the goals of the exam contribute to ex:Mission_V2 (the statement the exam work serves). COST OF THE ROUTE: seven register versions and commits for the revision, one for the closure of the fourth lineage, and the loss of the pointer purity (the lineage's mission pointer names the superseded statement; the owner may ask for a LineageRestart or a pointer move with a full rebuild of all five outputs). THE COST OF THE FOURTH LINEAGE (disclosed): the lineage agent advanced the fourth lineage (ex:Lineage4, mission ex:Mission_Midterm) from LS_Opened to LS_Backlogged in the versions 0.618.0 to 0.623.0 BEFORE the owner answered the route question (his rule: one lineage at a time, a different mission waits at Opened; he had asked whether the mission and scope already match the exam scope). That was a process slip. What it cost: (1) five register versions and six commits (9f8d8dc, dbf2ace, a55608b, a860120, e049103, 655adfc) that carry two active lineages with no link between them, which the shape UnconnectedActiveLineagesShape would report as a Violation; the full validator was not run on them; (2) a Mission, Scope, four goals, an objective, seven Proposed stories with criteria, tasks and planning events, and two planned iterations that have to be set down (lineage 4) and re-admitted (lineage 3); (3) the work of recomputing five digests with the digest table v5, which the third lineage does not use. Nothing was started, no urgent interruption was declared, no executor was briefed, and no committed file was edited; the forks stay in git as history." .
<http://example.org/sen0401-slides-lineage#AsIs_1> a backlog:AsIsAssessment ; backlog:assessesLineage <http://example.org/sen0401-slides-lineage#Lineage4> ;
    backlog:assessedAt "2026-10-29T14:35:25Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> ;
    backlog:hasFitGapStatement "AS-IS (2026-10-29): the fourth lineage was taken from LS_Opened to LS_Backlogged (Mission, Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog stages) before the owner's answer to the route question. It holds seven Proposed stories with their tasks, criteria and planning events in two planned iterations; nothing was started. FIT: the exam scope (the critical points, the general engine, the items, the paper rules, the papers, the grading method) is what the owner asked for. GAP: the lineage is a separate lineage for the same course; the owner's rule is one lineage at a time and his answer was that the exam scope belongs to the mission of the course, amended, and the lineage updated. The owner's correction (the chapter list is not fixed to 1 to 8) also makes its wording wrong. Its content is re-admitted in the third lineage (ex:Mission_V2, a stage revision from the Scope stage) in the versions that follow this one." ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "IMPACT: no item was started; the seven stories, the fourteen tasks, the criteria and the planning events of the fourth lineage are due and are not carried: the same items are admitted again, renamed, in the third lineage. Nothing is lost that was built, because nothing was built. The cost of the early advance is in ex:IA3_ExamMission. The lineage and its mission ex:Mission_Midterm stay in the register as history." ;
