    backlog:reportsCancelledItem ex:ST_Mid_CriticalPoints, ex:TK_Mid_CriticalPoints_Build, ex:TK_Mid_CriticalPoints_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_PaperRules, ex:TK_Mid_PaperRules_Build, ex:TK_Mid_PaperRules_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_Engine, ex:TK_Mid_Engine_Build, ex:TK_Mid_Engine_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_AnswerMethods, ex:TK_Mid_AnswerMethods_Build, ex:TK_Mid_AnswerMethods_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_Items, ex:TK_Mid_Items_Build, ex:TK_Mid_Items_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_Papers, ex:TK_Mid_Papers_Build, ex:TK_Mid_Papers_Verify, ex:ST_Mid_Grading, ex:TK_Mid_Grading_Build, ex:TK_Mid_Grading_Verify ;
    backlog:hasClosureMark backlog:Cm_Cancelled ; backlog:citesAssessment <http://example.org/sen0401-slides-lineage#AsIs_1> ; backlog:hasClosureSummary "Cancelled on 2026-10-29. The owner answered the route question: the exam scope is covered by amending the mission of the course and updating its lineage, not by a separate lineage, and he corrected the chapter scope. The fourth lineage was advanced to LS_Backlogged before that answer (a disclosed slip; see ex:IA3_ExamMission). Its exam chain is re-admitted in the third lineage under ex:Mission_V2. The mission ex:Mission_Midterm is kept as history." .
ex:Lineage4 rdfs:comment "Set down on 2026-10-29 by the closure report ex:Closure_5 (marked cancelled) after the as-is assessment AsIs_1. THE COST OF THE FOURTH LINEAGE (disclosed): the lineage agent advanced the fourth lineage (ex:Lineage4, mission ex:Mission_Midterm) from LS_Opened to LS_Backlogged in the versions 0.618.0 to 0.623.0 BEFORE the owner answered the route question (his rule: one lineage at a time, a different mission waits at Opened; he had asked whether the mission and scope already match the exam scope). That was a process slip. What it cost: (1) five register versions and six commits (9f8d8dc, dbf2ace, a55608b, a860120, e049103, 655adfc) that carry two active lineages with no link between them, which the shape UnconnectedActiveLineagesShape would report as a Violation; the full validator was not run on them; (2) a Mission, Scope, four goals, an objective, seven Proposed stories with criteria, tasks and planning events, and two planned iterations that have to be set down (lineage 4) and re-admitted (lineage 3); (3) the work of recomputing five digests with the digest table v5, which the third lineage does not use. Nothing was started, no urgent interruption was declared, no executor was briefed, and no committed file was edited; the forks stay in git as history."@en .
