ex:Revision_Lineage3_Scope30 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Scope stage: the exam work under the amended mission, and the page measurement of the chapters in the order the owner gave"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Scope ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ExamMission, ex:IA3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change request ex:CR3_ExamMission (Thursday 2026-10-29, the owner's words relayed by the coordinator (mission input 15:08 Istanbul; the owner's correction of the chapter scope and of the route the same day)) adds the exam deliverables and the page measurement of chapters 1 to 8 to a lineage whose Backlog stage is closed; a deliverable added to a closed scope statement is a revision from the Scope stage (ruling G127). The Mission stage is NOT revised: the amendment of the mission is route (c) and the superseding statement ex:Mission_V2 is not owned by the lineage, so the Mission output still reproduces. This version retracts the Scope, Goal, Objective and Backlog outputs and rebuilds nothing; the next four versions rebuild them one stage each, a sixth fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission under the new Backlog output." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_ScopeR29, ex:Out3_GoalR29, ex:Out3_ObjectiveR29, ex:Out3_BacklogR31 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "4decbc4" .
ex:SC3_Exam a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Scope grown: the exam work under the amended mission and the page measurements in the owner's order"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_ExamMission ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Exam_CriticalPoints, ex:ST_Exam_PaperRules, ex:ST_Exam_Engine, ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods, ex:ST_Exam_Items, ex:ST_Exam_Papers, ex:ST_Exam_Grading, ex:ST_Ch01_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch02_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch03_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch04_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch05_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch06_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch07_PageMeasure, ex:ST_Ch08_PageMeasure ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Decided by the owner in his explicit words of 2026-10-29 (Thursday 2026-10-29, the owner's words relayed by the coordinator (mission input 15:08 Istanbul; the owner's correction of the chapter scope and of the route the same day)): the exam scope is covered by amending the mission and updating the lineage; the chapter work is ordered (pages of chapters 1 to 6 measured first). Applied by the lineage agent. The boundary moved outward by 15 stories; new files only." .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-29 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_Exam and the stories it admits, on the owner's explicit word of 2026-10-29; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "THE VERIFIED GAPS G1 TO G7, which the exam deliverables, goals and criteria cite (carried over from the fourth lineage, where they were measured on 2026-10-29 by the lineage agent; the chapter numbers are the eight chapters then measured): VERIFIED GAPS (measured 2026-10-29 by the lineage agent on the repository as it stands): (G1) the exam engines are chapter specific: each of the 8 pages carries its own exam mode (screen based, started with a release code) over its own bank; no item belongs to more than one chapter (the bank field concept names one concept) and no engine builds an exam across chapters. (G2) the 8 banks hold 1,453 items, ALL single-answer four-option multiple choice (no fill-in, matching, ordering, calculation or written item); the levels are Remember 322, Understand 413, Apply 483, Analyze 235; Apply and Analyze together are 49.4 percent, Analyze alone 16.2 percent; chapter 8 holds 127 items, all Remember; chapter 6 has no Analyze item and chapter 7 has two; the answer letters are even except chapter 8 (30, 41, 25, 31); the correct option is the longest in 31.6 percent of items (chance is 25). (G3) nothing prints an exam: the pages' print styles only hide the interface; there is no paper layout, no two-version builder, no page-reduction method, no answer sheet. (G4) nothing reads or grades a paper: no scanning, reading, key matching or grading tool exists in the repository; the Exam Studio toolset (renderer, 19 quality gates, grading pipeline, CATS export) is NOT in this repository. (G5) the critical points the owner explained are not recorded as such anywhere: no slide, note or bank item carries such a mark. (G6) cross-chapter, synthesis and indirect items do not exist (0 of 1,453). (G7) nothing in the repository tests an item for fabricated terms or for needing course knowledge; the bank check tool covers the structure of the banks only."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "OWNER DECISION of 2026-10-30, relayed by the coordinator: the chapter lists keep the defaults. SEN0401: chapters 1 to 6 are the exam chapters; chapter 7 is NOT in. (The engine's chapter list stays a parameter with the default 1-6; chapter 7 stays selectable but is not used.) The decision for SEN0414 (chapters 1 to 8 without the chapter 5 debugging) belongs to that course's own register and is not recorded here. This closes the doubt about chapter 7 recorded in the owner statements above."@en .
ex:CR3_AnswerRepair a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Answer sheet reader: no silent wrong answer and no faint mark read as empty, found by the control of the answering-methods task"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ExamMission, ex:IA3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Friday 2026-10-30, after the control of TK_Exam_AnswerMethods_Build (register v0.647), as relayed by the course coordinator at the owner's standing rule that a repair is registered through change management. Found by the control of 2026-10-29 (register v0.647; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter32/bridge_answering): the executor's own check C6 of the answer sheet and methods (commit 6e37b8e) FAILS on its own evaluation seeds (block 9000): one written number box is not detected as written, so the reader gives a silent wrong answer (criterion: none allowed); and eight faint marks are read as empty without a flag (its check prints the count but its criterion does not test it). The control re-ran the measurement with the executor's own C6 criteria on three seed blocks the executor did not use: no silent wrong answer there, so the written-box error is rare and seed-bound; but unflagged empty reads of faint marks occur in all four blocks (8, 4, 6 and 1: 19 in all), so that defect is systematic. A faint mark read as empty becomes a blank answer for a student without anyone being told, which is the same kind of harm as a silent wrong answer. Held share is 21 to 23 percent against the limit of 25 percent, so there is little room. The check digit, the sheet geometry, the one-page cost and the executor's own log all reproduced; the failure is in the reader and its measurement only. Rules applied: the standing rules: a repair is registered through change management in the active lineage and re-ranks the open items; nothing is waived; a gate, test, threshold or criterion changes only on the owner's explicit word. The task ex:TK_Exam_AnswerMethods_Build stays Suspended and its criterion ex:AC3E_Exam_AnswerMethods is not rewritten (G125, G133); the repair is a NEW story ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair with a new Build task, a new Verify task and a new criterion. THE NEW CRITERION KEEPS THE EXECUTOR'S C6 CRITERIA AND EVERY THRESHOLD UNCHANGED (no registration failure, no silent wrong answer, no missed ambiguous row, every code slip and swap detected, at most 25 percent of recoverable rows held for a person); it adds the requirement that no mark is read as empty without a flag, which the check prints but never tested. The repair is evaluated on the original seed block 9000 and on held-out blocks that the control chooses at control time and does not name in advance, so that the reader cannot be tuned on the evaluation seeds (calibration stays on the seeds 1000 to 1099 or on a new calibration block the executor names before the run). If the 25 percent limit cannot be met together with the other criteria, the result is reported as printed and the repair is named failing; the limit is not raised (it changes only on the owner's word). A new criterion is counted by the Backlog digest, so the route is a revision from the Backlog stage (G125 route 2). Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the new story is recorded." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
ex:IA3_AnswerRepair a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the repair of the answer sheet reader costs, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_AnswerRepair ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Found by the control of 2026-10-29 (register v0.647; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter32/bridge_answering): the executor's own check C6 of the answer sheet and methods (commit 6e37b8e) FAILS on its own evaluation seeds (block 9000): one written number box is not detected as written, so the reader gives a silent wrong answer (criterion: none allowed); and eight faint marks are read as empty without a flag (its check prints the count but its criterion does not test it). The control re-ran the measurement with the executor's own C6 criteria on three seed blocks the executor did not use: no silent wrong answer there, so the written-box error is rare and seed-bound; but unflagged empty reads of faint marks occur in all four blocks (8, 4, 6 and 1: 19 in all), so that defect is systematic. A faint mark read as empty becomes a blank answer for a student without anyone being told, which is the same kind of harm as a silent wrong answer. Held share is 21 to 23 percent against the limit of 25 percent, so there is little room. The check digit, the sheet geometry, the one-page cost and the executor's own log all reproduced; the failure is in the reader and its measurement only. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog digest of the third lineage once, when the stage is closed again (one more story, two tasks, one criterion, one planning event, one iteration); Scope, Goal and Objective digests do not move. NEW ITEMS: the story ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair (it satisfies ex:Del3_ExamPapers and pursues ex:Obj3_Exam like the story it repairs), the tasks ex:TK_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair_Build and ex:TK_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair_Verify, the criterion ex:AC3E_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair, planned into the NEW iteration ex:Iter_50 (the goal of ex:Iter_48 is frozen at its start). The new files are a reader v1.1.0, a measurement and a check v1.1.0, as new files; the files of v1.0.0 are not edited. DEPENDENCIES CORRECTED: ex:TK_Exam_Papers_Build and ex:TK_Exam_Grading_Build read the sheet and the reader, so they now also wait for the repair Build task. THE SUSPENDED TASK: ex:TK_Exam_AnswerMethods_Build stays Suspended; how it reaches Done (a control over its own files together with the repair's files, against its own criterion unchanged) is decided at the control of the repair; nothing is waived. COST OF WAITING: papers whose answer sheets are read with a silent error and blank answers that no one is told about. COST OF ACTING: three register versions and one executor session of about three hours; the executor runs one at a time (disk), so the repair follows the engine executor, which is Done. Not affected: every Done item, the engine, the paper rules, the critical points, the committed files, the owner's questions Q1 to Q16." .
ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog7 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: the repair of the answer sheet reader found by the control"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_AnswerRepair, ex:IA3_AnswerRepair ;
    backlog:revisionReason "Found by the control of 2026-10-29 (register v0.647; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter32/bridge_answering): the executor's own check C6 of the answer sheet and methods (commit 6e37b8e) FAILS on its own evaluation seeds (block 9000): one written number box is not detected as written, so the reader gives a silent wrong answer (criterion: none allowed); and eight faint marks are read as empty without a flag (its check prints the count but its criterion does not test it). The control re-ran the measurement with the executor's own C6 criteria on three seed blocks the executor did not use: no silent wrong answer there, so the written-box error is rare and seed-bound; but unflagged empty reads of faint marks occur in all four blocks (8, 4, 6 and 1: 19 in all), so that defect is systematic. A faint mark read as empty becomes a blank answer for a student without anyone being told, which is the same kind of harm as a silent wrong answer. Held share is 21 to 23 percent against the limit of 25 percent, so there is little room. The check digit, the sheet geometry, the one-page cost and the executor's own log all reproduced; the failure is in the reader and its measurement only. The new acceptance criterion of the new story ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair is counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out3_BacklogR32 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it and a third fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission, not re-dated." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR32 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "d753769" .
ex:SC3_AnswerRepair a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Backlog widened by the repair of the answer sheet reader"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_AnswerRepair ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Decided by the owner through his standing rules (repairs are registered through change management in the active lineage and re-rank the open items; nothing is waived); applied by the lineage agent. A repair of delivered work found by the control, registered under the standing rules: a repair is registered through change management in the active lineage and re-ranks the open items; nothing is waived; a gate, test, threshold or criterion changes only on the owner's explicit word. Found by the control of 2026-10-29 (register v0.647; logs in 08-tooling/verify/iter32/bridge_answering): the executor's own check C6 of the answer sheet and methods (commit 6e37b8e) FAILS on its own evaluation seeds (block 9000): one written number box is not detected as written, so the reader gives a silent wrong answer (criterion: none allowed); and eight faint marks are read as empty without a flag (its check prints the count but its criterion does not test it). The control re-ran the measurement with the executor's own C6 criteria on three seed blocks the executor did not use: no silent wrong answer there, so the written-box error is rare and seed-bound; but unflagged empty reads of faint marks occur in all four blocks (8, 4, 6 and 1: 19 in all), so that defect is systematic. A faint mark read as empty becomes a blank answer for a student without anyone being told, which is the same kind of harm as a silent wrong answer. Held share is 21 to 23 percent against the limit of 25 percent, so there is little room. The check digit, the sheet geometry, the one-page cost and the executor's own log all reproduced; the failure is in the reader and its measurement only." .
ex:CR3_AnswerRepair rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-29 in the version that records the ScopeChange SC3_AnswerRepair and the story it admits; it was Pending before. The owner's standing rule is the decision: repairs are registered through change management and re-rank the open items."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "OWNER DECISION of 2026-10-30, relayed by the coordinator (owner questions Q8 and Q16): the answer mode is the SEPARATE BUBBLE GRID, one extra A4 page per student, machine-readable. Consequences: the answer sheet, its reader and the repair of the reader (ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair) stay in scope; the page cost of one more A4 page per student must be counted in every page count of the papers (the paper-rules page counts and any page limit include the sheet); circle-on-item is not the mode."@en .
ex:CR3_AnswerRepair rdfs:comment "OWNER DECISION of 2026-10-30, relayed by the coordinator (owner questions Q8 and Q16): the answer mode is the SEPARATE BUBBLE GRID, one extra A4 page per student, machine-readable. Consequences: the answer sheet, its reader and the repair of the reader (ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair) stay in scope; the page cost of one more A4 page per student must be counted in every page count of the papers (the paper-rules page counts and any page limit include the sheet); circle-on-item is not the mode."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "OWNER DECISION of 2026-10-30, relayed by the coordinator (owner question Q2, the count only): one SEN0401 midterm has 24 questions (a 60-minute sitting: fewer, longer synthesis and code-trace items, more thinking time per question); the make-up has the same count. THE CHAPTER WEIGHTS ARE NOT DECIDED: the working default is equal weight per chapter (4 items for each of chapters 1 to 6), which is the engine default and needs no evidence; it is not the only grounded choice: the weight could follow the number of critical points per chapter (12, 14, 19, 13, 20, 23 in the list of 2026-10-29), which gives 3, 3, 5, 3, 5, 5 items; the register holds no evidence of teaching hours per chapter. The owner decides if the default should change."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "OWNER DECISION of 2026-10-30, relayed by the coordinator (owner question Q7): the make-up NEVER reuses a midterm item. The engine's no-repeat rule (EN05) stays and stays a REFUSAL, not a warning. Note for the papers task: the engine of commit e662771 has an option --allow-repeat which the owner's decision makes unused; it is not to be used, and a later engine version may drop it as a new file."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamMission rdfs:comment "OWNER RULING of 2026-10-30 00:51 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator. The owner's words: 'Interactive page questions are accessible by the students before the exam. They are chapter subject specific questions, rarely cross-section. It is not wise to use them directly, but they can be a seed for better questions and enhancement iterations.' CONSEQUENCES, to be planned through change management: (1) no exam item may be a page item or a near copy of one; the engine gets a new rule, in SHACL, that refuses an item whose stem or option set matches a page-visible item, with a stated similarity method and a fixture of known answer (a new engine version as a new file, the old kept); (2) the page items serve as seeds: new, better items are built by enhancement iterations (change the situation, combine chapters, reverse the question, add a reasoning step, change the numbers), each new item linking its seed or seeds and the critical points it tests; (3) the bank report asks how many seeds exist per chapter and per critical point and what the seeds cannot give (cross-chapter, synthesis, calculation, reasoning); (4) all item types of the paper rules (matching, ordering, fill-in bank, number, trace) are authored items, not bank items. This replaces the earlier reading that the engine may compose papers from the bank items."@en .
ex:CR3_PageSeeds a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The page questions are seeds, not exam items: a rule that refuses a copy, and items built from seeds by enhancement iterations"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ExamMission, ex:IA3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Friday 2026-10-30, after the owner's ruling of 00:51 Istanbul, as relayed by the course coordinator. THE OWNER'S WORDS: 'Interactive page questions are accessible by the students before the exam. They are chapter subject specific questions, rarely cross-section. It is not wise to use them directly, but they can be a seed for better questions and enhancement iterations.' MEASURED by the seed report (08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_seedreport_v1_0_0.py, with a fixture of known answer; commit 0ebc134): the page-visible questions of chapters 1 to 6 are 1188 bank items (all four-option single-answer choice, 427 with a code listing; embedded in the pages as JSON; generators: chapters 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 one script each, chapter 3 none in 08-tooling) and 40 page quiz items; the pages also build their own exam desk (xExamBuild) from the concept tree, with kinds that are not enumerable as a list. The bank files were first committed on 2026-10-04 (chapters 1 to 5, commit 42764b2) and 2026-10-08 (chapter 6, 02da678); the generators write each item from a concept of the chapter ontology or a worked example whose program is run; no file of an earlier exam exists in the repository (the only files named exam, midterm or quiz outside the exam work are the page quiz files). Coverage of the 101 critical points of list A (chapters 1 to 6) by seed items, by a stated lexical method (two thresholds): 45 points with at least one seed at the strict threshold and 77 at the lenient one; per chapter strict [3, 8, 6, 8, 8, 12] of [12, 14, 19, 13, 20, 23] points. What the seeds are not: single-form (choice only; the banks hold no matching, ordering, fill-in, number or trace item), one concept each (every item comes from one concept of one chapter), and no item states a second chapter on purpose. The paper types of the page exam desk that suit paper: choice, matching, ordering, fill-in, trace; the desk's multi-select, true-or-false and run-code kinds do not. THE ENGINE OF COMMIT e662771 COMPOSES PAPERS FROM THE BANK ITEMS: under the owner's ruling that is what must not happen. WHAT CHANGES: (1) a NEW story ex:ST_Exam_NoCopy builds a new engine version (engine v1.1.0 as new files, v1.0.0 kept) with a new rule EN11 in SHACL that REFUSES any item whose stem or option set matches a page-visible item (the bank items and the page quiz items of the chapter list), with the similarity method and its thresholds stated before the run and a fixture of known answer; the engine builds papers from AUTHORED items only (no bank item is composed into a paper); all item types of the paper rules (choice, matching, ordering, fill-in bank, number, trace) are authored items; (2) the Items story is REVISED: it has not started, so its text and criterion are rewritten (G133 forbids that only while the work under a criterion runs): items are built from seeds by enhancement iterations (change the situation, combine chapters, reverse the question, add a reasoning step, change the numbers), and every item carries a link to its seed item(s) and to the critical point(s) it tests; (3) the seed report stays as the gap analysis the rules require before new work; (4) the Items Build task now waits for the new engine version, so that every item can be checked against EN11. A new criterion and rewritten text are counted by the Backlog digest, so the route is a revision from the Backlog stage (G125 route 2). Pending until the ScopeChange that admits the new story is recorded. Rules applied: the owner's ruling and the standing rules: gaps and changes go through change management in the active lineage; rulings are recorded in SHACL; nothing is waived." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .
ex:IA3_PageSeeds a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the seed ruling costs and touches, measured before it is started"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PageSeeds ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED by the seed report (08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_seedreport_v1_0_0.py, with a fixture of known answer; commit 0ebc134): the page-visible questions of chapters 1 to 6 are 1188 bank items (all four-option single-answer choice, 427 with a code listing; embedded in the pages as JSON; generators: chapters 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 one script each, chapter 3 none in 08-tooling) and 40 page quiz items; the pages also build their own exam desk (xExamBuild) from the concept tree, with kinds that are not enumerable as a list. The bank files were first committed on 2026-10-04 (chapters 1 to 5, commit 42764b2) and 2026-10-08 (chapter 6, 02da678); the generators write each item from a concept of the chapter ontology or a worked example whose program is run; no file of an earlier exam exists in the repository (the only files named exam, midterm or quiz outside the exam work are the page quiz files). Coverage of the 101 critical points of list A (chapters 1 to 6) by seed items, by a stated lexical method (two thresholds): 45 points with at least one seed at the strict threshold and 77 at the lenient one; per chapter strict [3, 8, 6, 8, 8, 12] of [12, 14, 19, 13, 20, 23] points. What the seeds are not: single-form (choice only; the banks hold no matching, ordering, fill-in, number or trace item), one concept each (every item comes from one concept of one chapter), and no item states a second chapter on purpose. The paper types of the page exam desk that suit paper: choice, matching, ordering, fill-in, trace; the desk's multi-select, true-or-false and run-code kinds do not. THE ENGINE OF COMMIT e662771 COMPOSES PAPERS FROM THE BANK ITEMS: under the owner's ruling that is what must not happen. WHAT MOVES: the Backlog digest of the third lineage once (one more story, two tasks, one criterion, one iteration; the Items story, tasks and criterion rewritten; one dependency added); Scope, Goal and Objective digests do not move. NOT AFFECTED: every Done item, the engine v1.0.0 and its check (it stays as a committed file), the paper rules (R01 to R22 stay), the answer sheet and its reader, the critical points, the owner's decisions of 2026-10-30 (24 questions per paper, the make-up never reuses an item, the bubble grid, chapters 1 to 6). COST OF THE ROUTE: one executor session of about three hours for the engine version (before the Items session), which delays the Items session by that time; the items session itself grows: items are authored, not chosen. COST OF NOT ACTING: papers built from questions the students have seen. THE ITEMS WORK IS LARGER THAN BEFORE: 48 authored items (24 per paper), each with seed and critical-point links, of types that the banks do not hold; the executor may need more than one session; that is estimated by the executor from the seed report and reported, not assumed." .
ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog8 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: the page questions are seeds, not exam items"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_PageSeeds, ex:IA3_PageSeeds ;
    backlog:revisionReason "MEASURED by the seed report (08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_seedreport_v1_0_0.py, with a fixture of known answer; commit 0ebc134): the page-visible questions of chapters 1 to 6 are 1188 bank items (all four-option single-answer choice, 427 with a code listing; embedded in the pages as JSON; generators: chapters 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 one script each, chapter 3 none in 08-tooling) and 40 page quiz items; the pages also build their own exam desk (xExamBuild) from the concept tree, with kinds that are not enumerable as a list. The bank files were first committed on 2026-10-04 (chapters 1 to 5, commit 42764b2) and 2026-10-08 (chapter 6, 02da678); the generators write each item from a concept of the chapter ontology or a worked example whose program is run; no file of an earlier exam exists in the repository (the only files named exam, midterm or quiz outside the exam work are the page quiz files). Coverage of the 101 critical points of list A (chapters 1 to 6) by seed items, by a stated lexical method (two thresholds): 45 points with at least one seed at the strict threshold and 77 at the lenient one; per chapter strict [3, 8, 6, 8, 8, 12] of [12, 14, 19, 13, 20, 23] points. What the seeds are not: single-form (choice only; the banks hold no matching, ordering, fill-in, number or trace item), one concept each (every item comes from one concept of one chapter), and no item states a second chapter on purpose. The paper types of the page exam desk that suit paper: choice, matching, ordering, fill-in, trace; the desk's multi-select, true-or-false and run-code kinds do not. THE ENGINE OF COMMIT e662771 COMPOSES PAPERS FROM THE BANK ITEMS: under the owner's ruling that is what must not happen. The new acceptance criterion and the rewritten Items story are counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out3_BacklogR33 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it and a third fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission, not re-dated." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR33 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "6c98a53" .
ex:SC3_PageSeeds a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Backlog widened by the seed ruling"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_PageSeeds ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Exam_NoCopy ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Decided by the owner in his ruling of 2026-10-30 00:51 Istanbul (the page questions are seeds, not exam items); applied by the lineage agent. MEASURED by the seed report (08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_seedreport_v1_0_0.py, with a fixture of known answer; commit 0ebc134): the page-visible questions of chapters 1 to 6 are 1188 bank items (all four-option single-answer choice, 427 with a code listing; embedded in the pages as JSON; generators: chapters 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 one script each, chapter 3 none in 08-tooling) and 40 page quiz items; the pages also build their own exam desk (xExamBuild) from the concept tree, with kinds that are not enumerable as a list. The bank files were first committed on 2026-10-04 (chapters 1 to 5, commit 42764b2) and 2026-10-08 (chapter 6, 02da678); the generators write each item from a concept of the chapter ontology or a worked example whose program is run; no file of an earlier exam exists in the repository (the only files named exam, midterm or quiz outside the exam work are the page quiz files). Coverage of the 101 critical points of list A (chapters 1 to 6) by seed items, by a stated lexical method (two thresholds): 45 points with at least one seed at the strict threshold and 77 at the lenient one; per chapter strict [3, 8, 6, 8, 8, 12] of [12, 14, 19, 13, 20, 23] points. What the seeds are not: single-form (choice only; the banks hold no matching, ordering, fill-in, number or trace item), one concept each (every item comes from one concept of one chapter), and no item states a second chapter on purpose. The paper types of the page exam desk that suit paper: choice, matching, ordering, fill-in, trace; the desk's multi-select, true-or-false and run-code kinds do not. THE ENGINE OF COMMIT e662771 COMPOSES PAPERS FROM THE BANK ITEMS: under the owner's ruling that is what must not happen." .
ex:CR3_PageSeeds rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-29 in the version that records the ScopeChange SC3_PageSeeds and the story it admits; it was Pending before. The owner's ruling is the decision."@en .
ex:CR3_MidtermFirst a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Build the midterm exam first; the make-up papers can wait"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Shrink ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_MidtermFirst, ex:CR3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "The owner, Friday 2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul, on the owner's word relayed by the coordinator, and the control of the urgent chapter 6 work by the lineage agent. THE OWNER'S WORD (2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul): return to the exams; the make-up papers can wait because the token budget is limited; build the MIDTERM first, the make-up later. THE EFFECT ON THE PLAN: the Items story now asks for the 24 items of the MIDTERM only (the make-up items, which must share none with them, become the new story ST_Exam_Items_Makeup, ranked behind, not dropped); the Papers story renders the midterm paper, its key and its answer sheet (the make-up paper becomes ST_Exam_Papers_Makeup); the grading story is unchanged (it reads any sheet). The engine keeps its rule that a make-up never repeats a midterm item, so the make-up items will be written against the finished midterm items. Nothing already measured changes." .
ex:IA3_MidtermFirst a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What building the midterm first costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_MidtermFirst ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORD (2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul): return to the exams; the make-up papers can wait because the token budget is limited; build the MIDTERM first, the make-up later. THE EFFECT ON THE PLAN: the Items story now asks for the 24 items of the MIDTERM only (the make-up items, which must share none with them, become the new story ST_Exam_Items_Makeup, ranked behind, not dropped); the Papers story renders the midterm paper, its key and its answer sheet (the make-up paper becomes ST_Exam_Papers_Makeup); the grading story is unchanged (it reads any sheet). The engine keeps its rule that a make-up never repeats a midterm item, so the make-up items will be written against the finished midterm items. Nothing already measured changes. AFFECTED: the Items story and its tasks (not started; midterm only, seed links and critical-point links on every item), the Papers story and its Build task (midterm paper), two new stories ST_Exam_Items_Makeup and ST_Exam_Papers_Makeup (ranked behind). NOT AFFECTED: the engine, the answer sheet, the grading story, every committed file. The plan: the engine v1.1.0 is controlled first, then the 24 midterm items, then the midterm paper; the make-up follows when the owner's budget allows. ESTIMATE (G120): the midterm items 6 h (unchanged), make-up items 6 h and make-up paper 1.5 h moved behind." .
ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog9 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: two chapter 6 repairs and the midterm first"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_Ch06Repairs, ex:CR3_MidtermFirst, ex:IA3_Ch06Repairs, ex:IA3_MidtermFirst ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change requests ex:CR3_Ch06Repairs, ex:CR3_MidtermFirst (Friday 2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul, on the owner's word relayed by the coordinator, and the control of the urgent chapter 6 work by the lineage agent) add four stories and rewrite the not-started Items and Papers stories' text and criterion; a new criterion is counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out3_BacklogR36 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it and a third fills the last commit; the items already in the register, Done ones included, re-enter by admission, not re-dated." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR36 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "865a32c" .
ex:SC3_Ch06Repairs a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Backlog widened by two repairs and the make-up split"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_Ch06Repairs, ex:CR3_MidtermFirst ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Exam_Items_Makeup, ex:ST_Exam_Papers_Makeup, ex:ST_Repair_Ch06_DeckLayout, ex:ST_Repair_Ch06_Lecture ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Decided by the owner (the midterm first, 2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul) and required by the repairs found in the delivered work; applied by the lineage agent. MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent on the delivered urgent work (deck v2_3_0, page v9.89.0, template 9.52.9). (1) THE LECTURE TAB: the page's data holds a lecture list of 62 entries, the manifest lecture_v1_3_1.json of the OLD 62-slide deck; the delivered deck v2_3_0 has 71 slides, so the Lecture tab does not show the deck the owner teaches from (the page executor reported it, my count agrees). (2) THE DECK LAYOUT: the deck layout check v1_0_0 prints 49 items to look at on v2_3_0 (for example slides 63, 65 and 67: 'needs 10.4 pt in 8.6 pt' for the RESULT line, 'needs 24.4 pt in 21.6 pt' for a caption) where v2_2_0 printed 'clean'; the new result lines and captions do not fit their boxes at the size the standard asks. The deck's code, results (52 of 52 re-run equal), prompts, lambda and label words are not in question. (3) PAGE TESTS: the executor reports that the committed page tests 9.34.2, 9.35.2 and 9.37.0 crash with StopIteration on the new page (the Playground now lists the slide examples first) while the copies 9.34.3, 9.35.3 and 9.38.0 pass; the lineage agent's own runs are recorded in the control note; whether the copies are accepted as the page tests is the owner's ruling and is asked through the coordinator. (4) NOT MEASURED, as printed: the deck standard check elements D3, D5 and D12 and the deck check example re-run read the '>>>' prompts and cannot read a prompt-free deck; the owner has allowed new reader files beside the old checks (old ones unchanged): this is the existing planned story ST_Code_Gate, which no longer waits for a further word. (5) RECONCILIATION NEEDED, not hidden: the urgent deck delivered most of what the planned stories ST_Ch06_DeckCode and ST_Ch06_DeckTeach and ST_Template_Panels were to deliver (code corrected, concepts told, panels and Playground); they are not started and their text, versions and dependencies no longer match what exists; they are closed or reduced by a fit-gap and closure step of their own. THE OWNER'S WORD (2026-10-30 07:45 Istanbul): return to the exams; the make-up papers can wait because the token budget is limited; build the MIDTERM first, the make-up later. THE EFFECT ON THE PLAN: the Items story now asks for the 24 items of the MIDTERM only (the make-up items, which must share none with them, become the new story ST_Exam_Items_Makeup, ranked behind, not dropped); the Papers story renders the midterm paper, its key and its answer sheet (the make-up paper becomes ST_Exam_Papers_Makeup); the grading story is unchanged (it reads any sheet). The engine keeps its rule that a make-up never repeats a midterm item, so the make-up items will be written against the finished midterm items. Nothing already measured changes." .
ex:CR3_MidtermFirst rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-30 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_Ch06Repairs; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:IA3_AnswerMethodsCancel a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "As-is fit-gap and impact of cancelling the answering-methods story"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_AnswerRepair ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "AS-IS FIT-GAP AND IMPACT ANALYSIS of ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods (read from the register v0.693.0; criterion AC3E_Exam_AnswerMethods; controls of 2026-10-29 and 2026-10-30). ACCOMPLISHED (met, measured): the answer sheet and the methods that reduce mistakes in giving answers exist as new files (commit 6e37b8e: one place per answer, a check digit, correction rules, a reader v1.0.0, a measurement on synthetic filled sheets); the owner decided the bubble grid answer sheet; the sheet is counted in the page count. FAILED (measured by the unit's own check C6 and by the control, register v0.647.0): the reader v1.0.0 did not detect one written box on the synthetic sheets, so the criterion of this unit was NOT MET; it was not waived. IN PROGRESS: nothing; the Build task is Suspended since the control and its Verify task was never started. DUE: nothing on this unit: what it was to deliver (a reader that gives no silent wrong reading) is carried by ex:ST_Exam_AnswerMethods_Repair (reader v1.1.0 with optical-density reading, no unflagged empty read of a faint mark, no silent wrong written box), Done on the control of the lineage agent on its own unnamed random blocks of 200 sheets (register v0.662.0, commit 4557301). IMPACT of the cancellation: the files and their commits stay unchanged; the criterion AC3E_Exam_AnswerMethods is not edited and not waived: it stays as the criterion this unit did not meet, and its measures are repeated by the criterion of the repair story. The Papers and Grading Build tasks (not started) lose the dependency on the cancelled Build task and keep the dependency on the repair Build task, which is Done. Nothing else changes." .
ex:CR3_BloomRule a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Higher Bloom level means Apply and above, with a minimum at Analyze and above"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_BloomRule, ex:CR3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "BLOOM RULE (owner's answer of 2026-10-30 about 10:30 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator): 'higher level' means Apply and above (use it, and work out why); AND at least 6 items at Analyze or above (work out why) per 24-item paper. The owner's own minimum for the 30-item SEN0414 paper is 8; the 6 for 24 items is a DEFAULT derived proportionally (8/30 x 24 = 6.4, rounded down), NOT the owner's word, to be confirmed by the owner when he sees the items. The majority of items is therefore at Apply or above, and the report names the count at Analyze or above. Chapter 6 has no Analyze item in the banks (seeds cannot give them): write those items new." .
ex:IA3_BloomRule a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the Bloom rule touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_BloomRule ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "BLOOM RULE (owner's answer of 2026-10-30 about 10:30 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator): 'higher level' means Apply and above (use it, and work out why); AND at least 6 items at Analyze or above (work out why) per 24-item paper. The owner's own minimum for the 30-item SEN0414 paper is 8; the 6 for 24 items is a DEFAULT derived proportionally (8/30 x 24 = 6.4, rounded down), NOT the owner's word, to be confirmed by the owner when he sees the items. The majority of items is therefore at Apply or above, and the report names the count at Analyze or above. Chapter 6 has no Analyze item in the banks (seeds cannot give them): write those items new. AFFECTED: the Items task and its criterion (not started; text rewritten, nothing waived); the Papers task reads the same rule through the engine. NOT AFFECTED: the engine (it already checks a Bloom majority), every committed file, the other stories. COST: none beyond the Items estimate; the chapter 6 Analyze items have no seed." .
ex:CR3_ReaderGap a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The reader v1.1.0 misses skipped-row shifts on the chapter-order layout"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_ReaderGap, ex:CR3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Friday 2026-10-30, on the report of the grading executor (commit a575006) and the lineage agent's own reproduction, and the control of the midterm paper. MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent with 08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_reader_gap_control_v1_0_0.py (logs verify/iter54/ctl/ctl_reader_gap_v1_1_0_reproduction.log): the COMMITTED reader v1.1.0 alone, on sheets of the midterm paper's CHAPTER-ORDER layout, lets a skipped-row shift cross a gap unflagged: seeds 41000-41039: 17 rows (7 of 40 sheets); seeds 52000-52199: 91 rows on 28 of 200 sheets; the grouped-by-type layout: 0 on both. The grading tool v1.0.0 adds two screens that hold the blocks across the gap (0 misses on 63000-63099 and 41000 in my own control), so a grade is protected, but the reader itself is not repaired. The earlier controls of the reader repair and of the paper (small sample, other layout) are corrected by an appended note (v0.722.0)." .
ex:CR3_PaperFormCode a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The two orders of the midterm paper print one form code, and a code box is too narrow for its longest line"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PaperFormCode, ex:CR3_ExamMission ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Friday 2026-10-30, on the report of the grading executor (commit a575006) and the lineage agent's own reproduction, and the control of the midterm paper. MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent: both orders of the midterm paper print the same form code 10100 on the answer sheet, so a scanned sheet carries nothing that tells which order's key it belongs to (the pair check refuses a key with the other order's layout, but a scanned sheet is graded against the key the instructor chooses). And on item 21 of the grouped order the 45-character line of the listing touches the right border of its code box (read on the rendered page; the executor's checks count characters, not the box). The owner has the grouped-order draft and decides the order and the cs_encode definition: the repair is built together with his changes to the items, as new files (a new items version and a renderer v1.3, never an edit)." .
ex:IA3_ReaderGap a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the reader gap costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ReaderGap ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent with 08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_reader_gap_control_v1_0_0.py (logs verify/iter54/ctl/ctl_reader_gap_v1_1_0_reproduction.log): the COMMITTED reader v1.1.0 alone, on sheets of the midterm paper's CHAPTER-ORDER layout, lets a skipped-row shift cross a gap unflagged: seeds 41000-41039: 17 rows (7 of 40 sheets); seeds 52000-52199: 91 rows on 28 of 200 sheets; the grouped-by-type layout: 0 on both. The grading tool v1.0.0 adds two screens that hold the blocks across the gap (0 misses on 63000-63099 and 41000 in my own control), so a grade is protected, but the reader itself is not repaired. The earlier controls of the reader repair and of the paper (small sample, other layout) are corrected by an appended note (v0.722.0). AFFECTED: one new repair story (the reader v1.2.0, new files); the grading story is Done and protected by its screens; the choice of the order of the paper (the grouped order gave no gap). NOT AFFECTED: every committed file. ORDER: the exams come first; the repair is ranked by the rank tool. ESTIMATE (G120): 3 h build, 1 h verification." .
ex:IA3_PaperFormCode a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the form code and the code box cost and touch"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PaperFormCode ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent: both orders of the midterm paper print the same form code 10100 on the answer sheet, so a scanned sheet carries nothing that tells which order's key it belongs to (the pair check refuses a key with the other order's layout, but a scanned sheet is graded against the key the instructor chooses). And on item 21 of the grouped order the 45-character line of the listing touches the right border of its code box (read on the rendered page; the executor's checks count characters, not the box). The owner has the grouped-order draft and decides the order and the cs_encode definition: the repair is built together with his changes to the items, as new files (a new items version and a renderer v1.3, never an edit). AFFECTED: one new repair story (new paper files, renderer v1.3, an items version if the owner changes an item). NOT AFFECTED: every committed file, the reader. ESTIMATE (G120): 2 h build, 1 h verification." .
ex:Revision_Lineage3_Backlog10 a backlog:StageRevision ;
    rdfs:label "Revision of the third lineage from the Backlog stage: two exam repairs"@en ;
    backlog:revisesLineage ex:Lineage3 ; backlog:revisesFromStage backlog:Stage_Backlog ;
    rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_ReaderGap, ex:CR3_PaperFormCode, ex:IA3_ReaderGap, ex:IA3_PaperFormCode ;
    backlog:revisionReason "The change requests ex:CR3_ReaderGap, ex:CR3_PaperFormCode (Friday 2026-10-30, on the report of the grading executor (commit a575006) and the lineage agent's own reproduction, and the control of the midterm paper) add two stories with their own criteria; a new criterion is counted by the Backlog digest, so the Backlog stage is revised (G125 route 2): this version retracts the Backlog output ex:Out3_BacklogR37 and rebuilds nothing; the next version rebuilds it and a third fills the last commit; the items already in it are re-admitted by the rebuilt output." ;
    backlog:retractsOutput ex:Out3_BacklogR37 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:revisedAtCommit "89c06a1c0c244dbc09a61f7324d591b0aafc742c" .
ex:SC3_ExamRepairs a backlog:ScopeChange ;
    rdfs:label "Backlog widened by the reader repair and the paper repair"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_ReaderGap, ex:CR3_PaperFormCode ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Repair_Exam_Reader, ex:ST_Repair_Exam_Paper ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "Required by the defects found in the delivered exam work and reproduced by the lineage agent; the rule that a repair enters the backlog and re-ranks the open items. MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent with 08-tooling/exam/sen0401_exam_reader_gap_control_v1_0_0.py (logs verify/iter54/ctl/ctl_reader_gap_v1_1_0_reproduction.log): the COMMITTED reader v1.1.0 alone, on sheets of the midterm paper's CHAPTER-ORDER layout, lets a skipped-row shift cross a gap unflagged: seeds 41000-41039: 17 rows (7 of 40 sheets); seeds 52000-52199: 91 rows on 28 of 200 sheets; the grouped-by-type layout: 0 on both. The grading tool v1.0.0 adds two screens that hold the blocks across the gap (0 misses on 63000-63099 and 41000 in my own control), so a grade is protected, but the reader itself is not repaired. The earlier controls of the reader repair and of the paper (small sample, other layout) are corrected by an appended note (v0.722.0). MEASURED 2026-10-30 by the lineage agent: both orders of the midterm paper print the same form code 10100 on the answer sheet, so a scanned sheet carries nothing that tells which order's key it belongs to (the pair check refuses a key with the other order's layout, but a scanned sheet is graded against the key the instructor chooses). And on item 21 of the grouped order the 45-character line of the listing touches the right border of its code box (read on the rendered page; the executor's checks count characters, not the box). The owner has the grouped-order draft and decides the order and the cs_encode definition: the repair is built together with his changes to the items, as new files (a new items version and a renderer v1.3, never an edit)." .
ex:CR3_ReaderGap rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-30 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_ExamRepairs; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_PaperFormCode rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-10-30 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_ExamRepairs; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_PaperWordFourPages a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The midterm paper is 4 pages in total, mixed order, and the paper, key and answer sheet are MS Word files"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PaperWordFourPages, ex:CR3_ExamMission, ex:CR3_PaperFormCode ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Sunday 2026-11-01, on the owner's words of 11:52 Istanbul time relayed by the coordinator. THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 and the day before): 'I need the PPT slides and interactive HTML files for both courses. Midterm scope: SEN0401: Chapters 1-6 ... the MS Word midterm exams, answer sheets. I will give you some details about the exam questions, as I made some interactive sessions during the class and ask them questions to understand if the students are reached to a certain level. The examinations should be developed to fit into 4 pages in total, to print in 2 pages, easy to read and assess, but using various techniques, including calculations, ordering, etc, that can be helpful to replace hand writing answers.' Earlier: '4 Pages to fit into 2 pages double side print. Mixed order mixed questions.' and 'Not PDF, MS Explorer for edit option'. MEASURED 2026-11-01 by the lineage agent on the committed items (23 items, 24 units) and renderer v1.2.0: the paper alone fills 4.2 to 4.4 content pages at the committed settings; with every layout lever together (margin 10 mm, leading 1.12, code 8 pt, item gap 1.0 mm, column gap 6 mm; text stays at 10 pt) it still fills 3.31 (chapter order) and 3.47 (grouped by type) content pages, i.e. 4 pages. So 3 content pages plus 1 answer-sheet page is NOT reachable by layout alone: the items must be shorter or fewer (about 10 to 15 percent less text), or the answer sheet must share a page with the last paper page. The paper rules (R01 text at least 10 pt, code at least 8 pt; R17 columns; R10 code capacity) are not changed." .
ex:IA3_PaperWordFourPages a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the four-page, mixed-order, Word paper costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PaperWordFourPages ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 and the day before): 'I need the PPT slides and interactive HTML files for both courses. Midterm scope: SEN0401: Chapters 1-6 ... the MS Word midterm exams, answer sheets. I will give you some details about the exam questions, as I made some interactive sessions during the class and ask them questions to understand if the students are reached to a certain level. The examinations should be developed to fit into 4 pages in total, to print in 2 pages, easy to read and assess, but using various techniques, including calculations, ordering, etc, that can be helpful to replace hand writing answers.' Earlier: '4 Pages to fit into 2 pages double side print. Mixed order mixed questions.' and 'Not PDF, MS Explorer for edit option'. MEASURED 2026-11-01 by the lineage agent on the committed items (23 items, 24 units) and renderer v1.2.0: the paper alone fills 4.2 to 4.4 content pages at the committed settings; with every layout lever together (margin 10 mm, leading 1.12, code 8 pt, item gap 1.0 mm, column gap 6 mm; text stays at 10 pt) it still fills 3.31 (chapter order) and 3.47 (grouped by type) content pages, i.e. 4 pages. So 3 content pages plus 1 answer-sheet page is NOT reachable by layout alone: the items must be shorter or fewer (about 10 to 15 percent less text), or the answer sheet must share a page with the last paper page. The paper rules (R01 text at least 10 pt, code at least 8 pt; R17 columns; R10 code capacity) are not changed. AFFECTED: the not-started story ST_Repair_Exam_Paper and its two tasks and criterion are rewritten (G133: nothing is started); the Done Papers story and its files are kept as the record. A .docx answer sheet cannot be proven to print in Word the way LibreOffice renders it: the sheet is built with fixed geometry, its layout is measured on the render, and the reader gets a stated scan tolerance. The items stay seeds until the owner passes the question styles of his class sessions; the reader repair (ST_Repair_Exam_Reader, unchanged) must be committed before the final build of the paper. NOT AFFECTED: every committed file, the grading tool, the reader story. OPEN FOR THE OWNER: whether the answer sheet may share a page with the paper, whether a second form with another mix is wanted, the cs_encode definition, the 24 items, the default of 6 at Analyze+, and the question styles. ESTIMATE (G120): 5 h build (was 2 h), 1.5 h verification." .
