ex:CR3_PaperSheetPdf a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The midterm paper is 3 Word pages plus a 1-page PDF answer sheet, mixed order"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_PaperSheetPdf, ex:CR3_ExamMission, ex:CR3_PaperFormCode, ex:CR3_PaperWordFourPages ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Sunday 2026-11-01, on the owner's answer 'Sheet stays PDF' relayed by the coordinator (to the sheet question after his words of 11:52). THE OWNER'S ANSWER: 'Sheet stays PDF' = paper and key in Word (.docx), the answer sheet a position-exact PDF (safest for scanning); four pages in total = 3 paper pages (Word) + 1 sheet page (PDF), printed double sided on 2 sheets, so the paper must fit 3 pages. THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 and the day before): 'I need the PPT slides and interactive HTML files for both courses. Midterm scope: SEN0401: Chapters 1-6 ... the MS Word midterm exams, answer sheets. I will give you some details about the exam questions, as I made some interactive sessions during the class and ask them questions to understand if the students are reached to a certain level. The examinations should be developed to fit into 4 pages in total, to print in 2 pages, easy to read and assess, but using various techniques, including calculations, ordering, etc, that can be helpful to replace hand writing answers.' Earlier: '4 Pages to fit into 2 pages double side print. Mixed order mixed questions.' and 'Not PDF, MS Explorer for edit option'. MEASURED 2026-11-01 by the lineage agent on the committed items (23 items, 24 units) and renderer v1.2.0: the paper alone fills 4.2 to 4.4 content pages at the committed settings; with every layout lever together (margin 10 mm, leading 1.12, code 8 pt, item gap 1.0 mm, column gap 6 mm; text stays at 10 pt) it still fills 3.31 (chapter order) and 3.47 (grouped by type) content pages, i.e. 4 pages. So 3 content pages plus 1 answer-sheet page is NOT reachable by layout alone: the items must be shorter or fewer (about 10 to 15 percent less text), or the answer sheet must share a page with the last paper page. The paper rules (R01 text at least 10 pt, code at least 8 pt; R17 columns; R10 code capacity) are not changed." .
ex:IA3_PaperSheetPdf a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the 3 Word pages plus 1 PDF sheet page cost and touch"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PaperSheetPdf ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S ANSWER: 'Sheet stays PDF' = paper and key in Word (.docx), the answer sheet a position-exact PDF (safest for scanning); four pages in total = 3 paper pages (Word) + 1 sheet page (PDF), printed double sided on 2 sheets, so the paper must fit 3 pages. THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 and the day before): 'I need the PPT slides and interactive HTML files for both courses. Midterm scope: SEN0401: Chapters 1-6 ... the MS Word midterm exams, answer sheets. I will give you some details about the exam questions, as I made some interactive sessions during the class and ask them questions to understand if the students are reached to a certain level. The examinations should be developed to fit into 4 pages in total, to print in 2 pages, easy to read and assess, but using various techniques, including calculations, ordering, etc, that can be helpful to replace hand writing answers.' Earlier: '4 Pages to fit into 2 pages double side print. Mixed order mixed questions.' and 'Not PDF, MS Explorer for edit option'. MEASURED 2026-11-01 by the lineage agent on the committed items (23 items, 24 units) and renderer v1.2.0: the paper alone fills 4.2 to 4.4 content pages at the committed settings; with every layout lever together (margin 10 mm, leading 1.12, code 8 pt, item gap 1.0 mm, column gap 6 mm; text stays at 10 pt) it still fills 3.31 (chapter order) and 3.47 (grouped by type) content pages, i.e. 4 pages. So 3 content pages plus 1 answer-sheet page is NOT reachable by layout alone: the items must be shorter or fewer (about 10 to 15 percent less text), or the answer sheet must share a page with the last paper page. The paper rules (R01 text at least 10 pt, code at least 8 pt; R17 columns; R10 code capacity) are not changed. AFFECTED: the not-started story ST_Repair_Exam_Paper and its two tasks and criterion are rewritten again (G133: nothing is started; it supersedes the rewrite of v0.730, which asked for a Word sheet); the owner chose the PDF sheet, the safest for scanning, so the Word-sheet verification falls away and the page budget becomes 3 paper pages. The paper's page count in Word cannot be proven here: it is measured on the LibreOffice render with a margin. The cs_encode item is decided from the chapter's facts (defined inside the item), not by the owner. The items stay seeds until the owner passes the question styles of his class sessions; the reader repair (ST_Repair_Exam_Reader, unchanged) must be committed before the final build of the paper. NOT AFFECTED: every committed file, the grading tool, the reader story. OPEN FOR THE OWNER: whether the answer sheet may share a page with the paper, whether a second form with another mix is wanted, the cs_encode definition, the 24 items, the default of 6 at Analyze+, and the question styles. ESTIMATE (G120): 5 h build, 1.5 h verification (unchanged from v0.730)." .
