    rdfs:label "What the midterm-scope quality work costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_MidtermQuality ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:13): 'Do you think the files you provided are ready to share? The source codes in the slides should match with the interactive page of that chapter's Chapter Examples in the Lab. You need to bring the files to the quality level of the files we have generated in our last Friday work and adapt all Midterm scope to this level before sharing them.' The coordinator's answer to him: NO. Midterm scope: SEN0401 chapters 1 to 6, to the chapter 6 Friday standard: prompt-free code, no untaught lambda, indented code, slides that teach alone, 5N1K as storytelling, the code on the slides equal to the page's Chapter Examples in slide order, on the page zoom, full screen and a resizable panel for every diagram, a Lecture tab matching the deck, a clean layout. The exam executors already running (reader, paper) continue. AS-IS FIT-GAP, MEASURED 2026-11-01 by the lineage agent on the newest deck and page of each chapter (prompts = '>>>' and '...' lines in slide text; deck layout check v1_0_0; page 'chaptercode' examples against the code-font slides in order, prompts ignored; Lecture tab = number of slides listed; 'full' = occurrences of fullscreen in the page): Ch1: deck SEN0401_Ch01_Introduction_3e_v3_2_0 (62 slides), prompt lines 62, lambdas on slides 0, label-word shapes 27, notes average 37 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch01_page_v9_73_0.html: examples 15 of 15 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 0; Lecture tab 62 of 62 slides; full screen 0. Ch2: deck SEN0401_Ch02_HowBitcoinWorks_3e_v3_0_0 (35 slides), prompt lines 50, lambdas on slides 3, label-word shapes 0, notes average 35 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch02_page_v9_72_0.html: examples 14 of 14 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 2; Lecture tab 35 of 35 slides; full screen 0. Ch3: deck SEN0401_Ch03_BitcoinCore_3e_v3_0_0 (42 slides), prompt lines 64, lambdas on slides 1, label-word shapes 0, notes average 36 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch03_page_v9_73_0.html: examples 19 of 19 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 1; Lecture tab 42 of 42 slides; full screen 0. Ch4: deck SEN0401_Ch04_KeysAndAddresses_3e_v3_4_0 (47 slides), prompt lines 67, lambdas on slides 4, label-word shapes 0, notes average 37 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch04_page_v9_74_0.html: examples 21 of 21 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 3; Lecture tab 47 of 47 slides; full screen 0. Ch5: deck SEN0401_Ch05_WalletRecovery_3e_v3_4_0 (68 slides), prompt lines 163, lambdas on slides 2, label-word shapes 0, notes average 35 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch05_page_v9_84_0.html: examples 27 of 27 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 2; Lecture tab 68 of 68 slides; full screen 0. Ch6: deck SEN0401_Ch06_Transactions_3e_v2_3_0 (71 slides), prompt lines 0, lambdas on slides 0, label-word shapes 12, notes average 44 words; layout check 49 item(s) to look at; page sen0401_ch06_page_v9_89_0.html: examples 2 of 20 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 0; Lecture tab 62 of 71 slides; full screen 5. FIT: the notes of every deck pass the notes check; the Lecture tab of chapters 1 to 5 equals the deck; the examples of chapters 1 to 5 are the slide code without prompts (15, 14, 19, 21 and 27 examples, all matched). GAP: prompts and lambdas on the slides of chapters 1 to 5 (so the slide code is not the page's Chapter Examples text); chapter 1 has label-word shapes; the notes are short but say little (the standard asks for clues); no page of chapters 1 to 5 offers full screen; chapter 6: the page is built from an older deck (18 examples and a Lecture tab of 62 slides against a deck of 71 slides and 20 code slides: only 2 examples match in order) and the deck has 49 layout items to look at. ROUTE: a change request in the running lineage, not an urgency ceremony: the exam executors that run (the reader and the paper) are not paused, the owner's exam-first rule of 2026-10-30 stays for them, and nothing is suspended; the work of chapters 1 to 6 is already planned as stories (the code-only deck, the page rebuild, the page measure, the deck checks, the code gate, the page templates) and this change adds what the Friday standard has that they lack: a Teach story for each of chapters 1 to 5 (slides that teach alone, storytelling, results as visuals, clean layout), the Lecture tab and the full-screen and resizable panels as criteria of the page rebuild, and the order. AFFECTED: five new stories ST_Ch01_DeckTeach to ST_Ch05_DeckTeach; the PageCode Build tasks of chapters 1 to 6 wait for the final deck of their chapter (and the chapter 6 Lecture repair waits for the chapter 6 Teach deck, since the slide count may change). NOT AFFECTED: every committed file, the exam stories. ESTIMATE (G120), agent hours per chapter: foundations (deck checks 4, code gate 4, code template 6, panels template 7) = 21; chapter 1: code deck 2.5 + Teach 8.5 + page 3 + measure 3 = 17; chapter 2: 2.5 + 5 + 3 + 3 = 13.5; chapter 3: 3 + 6 + 3 + 3 = 15; chapter 4: 3 + 6.5 + 3 + 3 = 15.5; chapter 5: 5 + 9.5 + 4 + 3 = 21.5; chapter 6: code deck 4 + Teach 10 + page 3 + measure 3 + Lecture and layout repairs (see their records) in addition. Total about 103 agent hours beyond the chapter 6 repairs. OPEN FOR THE OWNER (one question): which chapter he teaches next, to order the chapters." .
