nCore_3e_v3_0_0 (42 slides), prompt lines 64, lambdas on slides 1, label-word shapes 0, notes average 36 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch03_page_v9_73_0.html: examples 19 of 19 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 1; Lecture tab 42 of 42 slides; full screen 0. Ch4: deck SEN0401_Ch04_KeysAndAddresses_3e_v3_4_0 (47 slides), prompt lines 67, lambdas on slides 4, label-word shapes 0, notes average 37 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch04_page_v9_74_0.html: examples 21 of 21 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 3; Lecture tab 47 of 47 slides; full screen 0. Ch5: deck SEN0401_Ch05_WalletRecovery_3e_v3_4_0 (68 slides), prompt lines 163, lambdas on slides 2, label-word shapes 0, notes average 35 words; layout check clean; page sen0401_ch05_page_v9_84_0.html: examples 27 of 27 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 2; Lecture tab 68 of 68 slides; full screen 0. Ch6: deck SEN0401_Ch06_Transactions_3e_v2_3_0 (71 slides), prompt lines 0, lambdas on slides 0, label-word shapes 12, notes average 44 words; layout check 49 item(s) to look at; page sen0401_ch06_page_v9_89_0.html: examples 2 of 20 code slides matched in order; examples with a lambda 0; Lecture tab 62 of 71 slides; full screen 5. FIT: the notes of every deck pass the notes check; the Lecture tab of chapters 1 to 5 equals the deck; the examples of chapters 1 to 5 are the slide code without prompts (15, 14, 19, 21 and 27 examples, all matched). GAP: prompts and lambdas on the slides of chapters 1 to 5 (so the slide code is not the page's Chapter Examples text); chapter 1 has label-word shapes; the notes are short but say little (the standard asks for clues); no page of chapters 1 to 5 offers full screen; chapter 6: the page is built from an older deck (18 examples and a Lecture tab of 62 slides against a deck of 71 slides and 20 code slides: only 2 examples match in order) and the deck has 49 layout items to look at." .
ex:CR3_MidtermQuality rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-11-01 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_MidtermQuality; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_MidtermQuality rdfs:comment "Owner, 2026-11-01 12:17: 'I will continue with Chapters 7-8 for SEN0401 and Chapters 9-10 for SEN0414 after the Midterm week on 15.11.2026.' CORRECTED by the owner at 12:19: 'No, you misunderstood. All the remaining content should start as soon as we finish the Midterm files including the exam, slides and interactive pages. The given date is a due, not a wait date.' So 15.11.2026 is the DUE date of SEN0401 Chapters 7-8 (and the remaining content); the order is: (1) the midterm files first (exam, slides, pages of chapters 1 to 6 to the Friday standard), (2) the moment they are finished Chapters 7-8 start (one lineage at a time), due before 15.11.2026. PLAN (agent hours, G120 estimates): exams in progress 8 (reader 3, paper 5); foundations 21 (deck checks 4, code gate 4, code template 6, panels template 7; critical path 17); chapters: 6 = 24.5, 5 = 21.5, 1 = 17, 4 = 15.5, 3 = 15, 2 = 13.5, total 107.0; midterm quality total 128; Chapters 7-8 about 32 (an estimate: they are not yet measured; the as-is fit-gap and their stories follow when the midterm files are finished). Recommended chapter order (gap size and exam value): 6, 5, 1, 4, 3, 2."@en .
ex:CR3_MidtermToday a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The midterm scope is restructured to start at once: dependencies on controls become dependencies on built files"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_MidtermToday, ex:CR3_MidtermQuality ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Sunday 2026-11-01, on the owner's words of 12:13 Istanbul time relayed by the coordinator. THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:2x Istanbul): 'Today we should finish both the Midterms and midterm scope work.' The target is today for the exams and chapters 1 to 6 at the Friday standard. The lineage agent cannot prove that about 136 agent hours fit in a day (the estimates are in ex:CR3_MidtermQuality); the work is therefore restructured for the most safe parallelism. REAL VS ORDERING: (1) the deck builds of chapters 1 to 6 need only the marker convention stated in the code-gate task (code boxes and result lines named by prefix), not the finished checks: the dependency on the code gate and the deck checks is moved from the Build to the Verify; (2) the Teach build of a chapter continues the deck of its DeckCode build in the same executor session (the same file lineage), so it depends on the DeckCode Build, not on its Verify; (3) the page of a chapter needs the final deck file and the panels template file, not their controls: it depends on the Teach Build and the Panels Build; (4) the page template 9.52.6 does not need the gate; the panels template 9.52.7 really extends 9.52.6 (a real dependency, on the Build). A Verify task is still required for every Done: if the control finds a defect after a dependent was built on the file, the defect is repaired as a new version and the dependent is rebuilt; that risk is accepted and named here." .
ex:IA3_MidtermToday a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the restructure costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_MidtermToday ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:2x Istanbul): 'Today we should finish both the Midterms and midterm scope work.' The target is today for the exams and chapters 1 to 6 at the Friday standard. The lineage agent cannot prove that about 136 agent hours fit in a day (the estimates are in ex:CR3_MidtermQuality); the work is therefore restructured for the most safe parallelism. REAL VS ORDERING: (1) the deck builds of chapters 1 to 6 need only the marker convention stated in the code-gate task (code boxes and result lines named by prefix), not the finished checks: the dependency on the code gate and the deck checks is moved from the Build to the Verify; (2) the Teach build of a chapter continues the deck of its DeckCode build in the same executor session (the same file lineage), so it depends on the DeckCode Build, not on its Verify; (3) the page of a chapter needs the final deck file and the panels template file, not their controls: it depends on the Teach Build and the Panels Build; (4) the page template 9.52.6 does not need the gate; the panels template 9.52.7 really extends 9.52.6 (a real dependency, on the Build). A Verify task is still required for every Done: if the control finds a defect after a dependent was built on the file, the defect is repaired as a new version and the dependent is rebuilt; that risk is accepted and named here. AFFECTED: the dependencies of 33 not-started tasks and the planned session of the Teach and panels Build tasks (set to the session of the build they continue). NOT AFFECTED: every criterion, every committed file, the exam stories that run. RISK: a defect found by a Verify after a dependent was built is repaired as a new version and the dependent rebuilt." .
