    rdfs:label "Dependencies of the midterm-scope tasks moved from the controls to the built files"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_MidtermToday ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Ch06_DeckCode ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:2x Istanbul): 'Today we should finish both the Midterms and midterm scope work.' The target is today for the exams and chapters 1 to 6 at the Friday standard. The lineage agent cannot prove that about 136 agent hours fit in a day (the estimates are in ex:CR3_MidtermQuality); the work is therefore restructured for the most safe parallelism. REAL VS ORDERING: (1) the deck builds of chapters 1 to 6 need only the marker convention stated in the code-gate task (code boxes and result lines named by prefix), not the finished checks: the dependency on the code gate and the deck checks is moved from the Build to the Verify; (2) the Teach build of a chapter continues the deck of its DeckCode build in the same executor session (the same file lineage), so it depends on the DeckCode Build, not on its Verify; (3) the page of a chapter needs the final deck file and the panels template file, not their controls: it depends on the Teach Build and the Panels Build; (4) the page template 9.52.6 does not need the gate; the panels template 9.52.7 really extends 9.52.6 (a real dependency, on the Build). A Verify task is still required for every Done: if the control finds a defect after a dependent was built on the file, the defect is repaired as a new version and the dependent is rebuilt; that risk is accepted and named here." .
