ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The midterm-scope tasks are simplified to the Friday fixes: reuse, no re-measuring, one session per chapter"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:IA3_MidtermSimplify, ex:CR3_MidtermQuality, ex:CR3_MidtermToday ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Raised Sunday 2026-11-01, on the owner's words of 12:13 Istanbul time relayed by the coordinator. THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:26 Istanbul): 'Simplify the tasks of the agents to concentrate on the issues we have solved on friday, and pass the useless effort spent to remeasure the allready succeeded parts.' The coordinator's reading: the work per chapter is exactly the Friday fixes (no '>>>' prompts, no untaught lambdas, indented code, slides that teach alone, 5N1K as storytelling, the slide code equal to the page's Chapter Examples in slide order, on the page full screen, a resizable panel and the Lecture tab), reusing the chapter 6 tools and templates; what passed is not measured again; the existing gates run ONCE at the end of a chapter; the foundation stories are dropped or merged unless reuse is impossible; one brief per chapter (deck and page together). THE FACTS (read by the lineage agent in the repository, 2026-11-01): the page template 9.52.9 (full screen and reader-set size for every diagram panel, slide examples first in the Playground, no prompt in the card), the page builder 4.19.0 and the panel test v1_0_0 were made on Friday and passed on the chapter 6 page v9.89.0 (page tests 9.34.3, 9.35.3, 9.38.0 PASS); so the stories ST_Code_Template (page template 9.52.6) and ST_Template_Panels (9.52.7) are satisfied by files that already exist and are CANCELLED by the next version with the fit-gap and a closure report, not rebuilt. The code gate and the four deck checks (indentation, lambda, label words, prompts) are NOT available as tools for chapters 1 to 5 (the committed deck checks find code by the prompts), so they stay, merged into one small session of 3 hours each. The chapter 6 deck v2_3_0 already has no prompts and no lambdas, so its DeckCode task is only a verification of 0.5 hours. NOT WEAKENED: every gate and every criterion stays; a gate that passed on unchanged bytes is not re-run (the cache of the method, R9), and each chapter's existing gates run once at its end (the PageMeasure task, about 1 hour). RISK named: the agents reuse the Friday builders; if a builder does not fit a chapter the executor stops and reports." .
ex:IA3_MidtermSimplify a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the simplification costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 12:26 Istanbul): 'Simplify the tasks of the agents to concentrate on the issues we have solved on friday, and pass the useless effort spent to remeasure the allready succeeded parts.' The coordinator's reading: the work per chapter is exactly the Friday fixes (no '>>>' prompts, no untaught lambdas, indented code, slides that teach alone, 5N1K as storytelling, the slide code equal to the page's Chapter Examples in slide order, on the page full screen, a resizable panel and the Lecture tab), reusing the chapter 6 tools and templates; what passed is not measured again; the existing gates run ONCE at the end of a chapter; the foundation stories are dropped or merged unless reuse is impossible; one brief per chapter (deck and page together). THE FACTS (read by the lineage agent in the repository, 2026-11-01): the page template 9.52.9 (full screen and reader-set size for every diagram panel, slide examples first in the Playground, no prompt in the card), the page builder 4.19.0 and the panel test v1_0_0 were made on Friday and passed on the chapter 6 page v9.89.0 (page tests 9.34.3, 9.35.3, 9.38.0 PASS); so the stories ST_Code_Template (page template 9.52.6) and ST_Template_Panels (9.52.7) are satisfied by files that already exist and are CANCELLED by the next version with the fit-gap and a closure report, not rebuilt. The code gate and the four deck checks (indentation, lambda, label words, prompts) are NOT available as tools for chapters 1 to 5 (the committed deck checks find code by the prompts), so they stay, merged into one small session of 3 hours each. The chapter 6 deck v2_3_0 already has no prompts and no lambdas, so its DeckCode task is only a verification of 0.5 hours. NOT WEAKENED: every gate and every criterion stays; a gate that passed on unchanged bytes is not re-run (the cache of the method, R9), and each chapter's existing gates run once at its end (the PageMeasure task, about 1 hour). RISK named: the agents reuse the Friday builders; if a builder does not fit a chapter the executor stops and reports. AFFECTED: the text, estimate and session of 27 not-started Build tasks and the dependencies of the page tasks; the two template stories are cancelled by the next version. ESTIMATE (G120), agent hours: code gate 3 and deck checks 3 (one session); chapter 1 = 2.5 + 5 + 2 + 1 = 10.5; chapter 2 = 8.5; chapter 3 = 9.5; chapter 4 = 10; chapter 5 = 15; chapter 6 = 0.5 + 6 + 2 + 1 + 2 (layout repair) + 0.5 (Lecture) = 12; total about 76 (was 136). NOT AFFECTED: every criterion, every committed file, the exam stories that run. RISK: the Friday builders may not fit a chapter (the executor stops and reports)." .
