ex:IA3_TemplatesCancel a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "As-is fit-gap and impact of cancelling the two page template stories"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "AS-IS FIT-GAP AND IMPACT ANALYSIS of ex:ST_Code_Template (page template 9.52.6) and ex:ST_Template_Panels (page template 9.52.7), both with Proposed tasks, read from the register v0.753.0. ACCOMPLISHED by existing files (read in the repository, 2026-11-01): the page template 9.52.9 exists (08-tooling/course_page_template_v9_52_9.html; 9.52.6 and 9.52.7 exist too), with full screen and a reader-set size for every diagram panel, the slide examples first in the Playground and no prompt in the card; the page builder 4.19.0 and the panel test v1_0_0 exist; the chapter 6 page v9.89.0 built on them passed the page tests 9.34.3, 9.35.3 and 9.38.0 and the panel test (commits b92453e, 0929f04, a3cbe63). FAILED: nothing is known to fail in these templates. IN PROGRESS: nothing. DUE: nothing of these two stories is due; chapters 1 to 5 reuse template 9.52.9 and builder 4.19.0 (the page tasks name them). IMPACT of the cancellation: no file changes; the criteria of the two stories are NOT claimed as met and not waived (the templates were made under the urgent chapter 6 work and not controlled through these stories); the page tasks of chapters 1 to 6 lost their dependency on ex:TK_Template_Panels_Build in v0.753.0 and name the template 9.52.9; the re-rank follows. If a chapter finds that 9.52.9 does not fit it, the executor stops and reports, and a new story is raised then." .
ex:CR3_ExamNewRules a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The exams get the IKU cover page, five question formats, no memorising items, tips and spelled-out abbreviations, in four pages or else six"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 13:04): 'Use the attached page and fill the generic parts appropriately for each of the exams. Categorize the exam into 5 question format with possible number of sub-questions. If possible 4 questions 25 points and 5th Question is 10 points and bonus. If you can fit overall exam in 4 pages it is fine, otherwise, fit with 6 pages but better formatting and readability. The abbreviations should be used in full form in their first usage. Never ask memorizing questions and dont force the students to remember a specific terminology. You should support the students with provide tips to remember, if you use a specific term in the exam. What SegWit scripts, P2PKH, ... are is not important, their usage and the importance for the Bitcoin the reason they exist is more important.' The attached page is the cover page of another IKU course (copy: /home/claude/exam_cover_template/IKU_exam_cover_page_template_source.docx). AUDIT (heuristic, by names only, 23 items of items v1.1.0): terms or abbreviations without expansion or tip appear in at least items i12, i14, i15, i19, i20; the full audit is the first element of the items task. HOW THE PAPER STORIES ARE REOPENED: ST_Repair_Exam_Paper and ST_Repair_Exam_Reader stay Done and are not edited (G125); the new stories make NEW items (v1.2.0), a cover renderer, papers, key and sheet v3 as new files; the reader is unchanged while the sheet's block types are unchanged. This supersedes the earlier target of 3 paper pages plus 1 sheet page, and the wait for the owner's question styles." .
