ex:CR3_ExamCases a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The exam items and papers take the owner's three cases and topic list from his class sessions"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 21:09 Istanbul, from his class sessions): three cases to turn into items, used as seeds with original wording and numbers, simple arithmetic without a calculator, no memorisation, a tip whenever a term is used. (1) ORDERING: a chain of successively spent transaction outputs; ask the order of the transactions; a spending transaction always comes after the transaction whose output it spends, traceable back to the coinbase transaction. (2) MINED OR NOT: a set of transactions with spending references; a transaction that receives a spending reference means the referenced transaction was already mined; ask which are mined and which are not (in the same question as 1 or separately). (3) FULL SPENDING: if no change output is added, the unspent difference is the fee and the miner collects it; ask the change amount (or the fee) of a transaction with several inputs and several outputs, with simple numbers. His earlier topic list, also relevant: serverless peer-to-peer; distributed trust; double-spending prevention; independent confirmations; approval without private keys (what a signature proves); telling a genuine from a fake transaction; timing differences in spending; why seed words replaced hand-managed random keys; the borderless nature of Bitcoin. He has not yet chosen between a topic map and his per-topic notes, so more notes may follow and the items task accepts additions. MAPPING AGAINST ITEMS v1.2.0 (reading the items in full): KEPT: i05 shop confirmations (independent confirmations and double-spending prevention), i23 fill txid and weight (chapter 6, no overlap with the three cases). REWORKED: i02 fee not written becomes case 3 (several inputs and outputs, the change amount or the fee, same four-choice answer block); i07 fill fee rate and set becomes case 2 (mined or not by spending references, and the unspent outputs that form the set, same fill-in answer block). REPLACED: i06 order wallet to block becomes case 1 (order of a spending chain back to the coinbase transaction, same ordering answer block). The other items stay unless the topic list shows a gap, which the executor reports and fills only by replacing, never by adding (the structure stays 25/25/25/25 + 10, one unit per sub-question). Done exam stories and tasks are not edited (G125)." .
ex:IA3_ExamCases a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the exam cases of the owner cost and touch"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ExamCases ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "THE OWNER'S WORDS (relayed, 2026-11-01 21:09 Istanbul, from his class sessions): three cases to turn into items, used as seeds with original wording and numbers, simple arithmetic without a calculator, no memorisation, a tip whenever a term is used. (1) ORDERING: a chain of successively spent transaction outputs; ask the order of the transactions; a spending transaction always comes after the transaction whose output it spends, traceable back to the coinbase transaction. (2) MINED OR NOT: a set of transactions with spending references; a transaction that receives a spending reference means the referenced transaction was already mined; ask which are mined and which are not (in the same question as 1 or separately). (3) FULL SPENDING: if no change output is added, the unspent difference is the fee and the miner collects it; ask the change amount (or the fee) of a transaction with several inputs and several outputs, with simple numbers. His earlier topic list, also relevant: serverless peer-to-peer; distributed trust; double-spending prevention; independent confirmations; approval without private keys (what a signature proves); telling a genuine from a fake transaction; timing differences in spending; why seed words replaced hand-managed random keys; the borderless nature of Bitcoin. He has not yet chosen between a topic map and his per-topic notes, so more notes may follow and the items task accepts additions. MAPPING AGAINST ITEMS v1.2.0 (reading the items in full): KEPT: i05 shop confirmations (independent confirmations and double-spending prevention), i23 fill txid and weight (chapter 6, no overlap with the three cases). REWORKED: i02 fee not written becomes case 3 (several inputs and outputs, the change amount or the fee, same four-choice answer block); i07 fill fee rate and set becomes case 2 (mined or not by spending references, and the unspent outputs that form the set, same fill-in answer block). REPLACED: i06 order wallet to block becomes case 1 (order of a spending chain back to the coinbase transaction, same ordering answer block). The other items stay unless the topic list shows a gap, which the executor reports and fills only by replacing, never by adding (the structure stays 25/25/25/25 + 10, one unit per sub-question). Done exam stories and tasks are not edited (G125). AFFECTED: two new stories with four tasks (about 7 agent-hours); the Done exam stories are not reopened (G125); the reader and the sheet stay unchanged while the block types stay." .
