ex:CR3_PlaygroundTests a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The page tests are proven on the Playground of the new pages"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "FINDING (lineage agent, quiet window, 2026-11-01/02): the committed page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.2 crash (StopIteration in the Playground step, after 27 features passed and 0 failed) on every page whose Playground lists the chapter's slide examples (the option values 'cc:N'), for example Ch02 v9_73_0. A gate that cannot run is not a pass. The versioned copies already exist and differ from the old tests by ONE line each: 9.34.3 over 9.34.2 and 9.38.0 over 9.37.0 (the expected code of an option whose value starts with 'cc:' is read from the page's chapter-code examples). WHAT TO DO (new files only; no gate is weakened, loosened or retuned; the committed tests are never edited): (1) Show by diff, as printed, that 9.34.3 and 9.38.0 differ from 9.34.2 and 9.37.0 only in that line, and that every other check is identical. (2) Build FIXTURES OF KNOWN ANSWER for that Playground step: a page copy in which the code of one 'cc:' option is altered (the step must FAIL, naming the option), a page copy with a 'cc:' value out of range (must FAIL, not crash), and the true page (must PASS); run 9.34.3 and 9.38.0 on each and report each result as printed. If a fixture shows that the step cannot fail when it should, report it as a defect and make a new versioned test (9.34.4 and 9.38.1, new files) that fails correctly. (3) Run 9.34.3 on the Ch01 v9_74_0, Ch02 v9_73_0 and Ch04 v9_75_0 pages, one at a time, each under flock /tmp/page_test.lock (the lineage agent has run 9.38.0 on them, not 9.34.3). (4) Run nothing else on the lock; delete scratch copies and temporary folders you create (disk stop at 0.9 GB free). (5) Report every result verbatim, including a failure, and the commit ids. " .
ex:IA3_PlaygroundTests a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the page-test fixtures cost and touch"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_PlaygroundTests ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "FINDING (lineage agent, quiet window, 2026-11-01/02): the committed page tests 9.37.0 and 9.34.2 crash (StopIteration in the Playground step, after 27 features passed and 0 failed) on every page whose Playground lists the chapter's slide examples (the option values 'cc:N'), for example Ch02 v9_73_0. A gate that cannot run is not a pass. The versioned copies already exist and differ from the old tests by ONE line each: 9.34.3 over 9.34.2 and 9.38.0 over 9.37.0 (the expected code of an option whose value starts with 'cc:' is read from the page's chapter-code examples). WHAT TO DO (new files only; no gate is weakened, loosened or retuned; the committed tests are never edited): (1) Show by diff, as printed, that 9.34.3 and 9.38.0 differ from 9.34.2 and 9.37.0 only in that line, and that every other check is identical. (2) Build FIXTURES OF KNOWN ANSWER for that Playground step: a page copy in which the code of one 'cc:' option is altered (the step must FAIL, naming the option), a page copy with a 'cc:' value out of range (must FAIL, not crash), and the true page (must PASS); run 9.34.3 and 9.38.0 on each and report each result as printed. If a fixture shows that the step cannot fail when it should, report it as a defect and make a new versioned test (9.34.4 and 9.38.1, new files) that fails correctly. (3) Run 9.34.3 on the Ch01 v9_74_0, Ch02 v9_73_0 and Ch04 v9_75_0 pages, one at a time, each under flock /tmp/page_test.lock (the lineage agent has run 9.38.0 on them, not 9.34.3). (4) Run nothing else on the lock; delete scratch copies and temporary folders you create (disk stop at 0.9 GB free). (5) Report every result verbatim, including a failure, and the commit ids.  AFFECTED: one new story with two tasks (about 2.5 agent-hours); the Verify tasks of the Ch01 to Ch04 PageCode stories depend on it (a gate that cannot run is not a pass); the open items are re-ranked (G147)." .
