ex:CR3_Ch03PageRepair2 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The chapter 3 page v9_74_0 is repaired as a new page"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "DEFECT (measured by the lineage agent, 2026-11-02, control of the repair page v9_75_0, test 9.38.0 unchanged, under one lock hold with the shipped v9_73_0 run straight after it, machine load average 6.4 at the start of the first run and 3.3 at the second): chapter 3 page v9_75_0 (the first repair) FAILS the main-thread budget feature: 396 passed 2 failed, load task median 145 ms of [131, 141, 145, 214] (bound 227, passes), but after load ONE main-thread task of 2063 ms (the printed 'after load' value is the longest task after 5000 ms; 28 long tasks in all). The shipped v9_73_0 in the next hold: 398 passed 0 failed, longest 143 ms. The executor's own two runs of v9_75_0 passed (after load 68 ms over 2 long tasks and 78 ms over 5), so the failure is intermittent or load dependent, and the first repair is not Done. KNOWN FROM THE FIRST REPAIR (its bisect logs in 08-tooling/ch03-page/page_9_75_0_logs/bisect/RESULTS.txt): on v9_74_0 the long tasks after load came from filling the 87 examples of the Playground loop (one pg.fill of TransactionSerialization = 1 beforeinput plus 99 input events, EventDispatch 450 ms, Layout 134 ms), the undoing of the plain-code data removed them (variants v1b, v5, v6 passed, v1 to v4 failed), and the final template cut one fill from about 440 ms to about 60 ms. HYPOTHESES to test, not to assume: (H1) the post-load work is still proportional to the CPU available, so a contended machine turns a 60 ms step into a very long one (a margin problem: the page does the work in one task instead of in slices); (H2) the 2063 ms task is a separate once-only step after 5000 ms (for example the first run of the embedded Python runtime, a layout of the ontology graph, the syntax highlighting of all listings, or garbage collection) that the first repair did not touch. " .
