ex:CR3_ExamV6Floor a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The paper total of both exams is floored at 0 (owner ruling)"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER RULING (2026-11-02, 16:52 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), the answer to the floor point raised with the sheet and scoring work of the exam v6: the total of the whole paper is floored at 0 for both exams (SEN0401 and SEN0414); there is no floor inside a question. For SEN0401 the printed paper, cover and sheet need no change if they do not state a floor (the lineage agent checked: the cover says a wrong answer can cost part of its points and a blank costs nothing; sheet page 2 says a blank answer costs nothing; neither states a total or a floor), but the instructor key and the scoring module's floor setting must say so. The measured figures before the ruling (lineage agent, 20000 blind sheets that mark every place, the v6 key of 100 points): mean of the raw total -0.05, mean of the floored total +3.65, 53 percent of the blind sheets fall below 0 and are floored; the owner's SEN0414 figure is about +4.3 of 110." .
