    rdfs:label "The exam v7: no deductions, no bonus, five alternatives, short tips, one-page sheet"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER REDESIGN (2026-11-02, 18:20 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), urgent, supersedes the floor and penalty work. The owner: the deduction calculations are too complicated and impossible by hand; each question's deduction is different, which confuses and stresses students; simplify, students may get advantages; the answer sheet with tips is 3 pages and the exam 6, total 9, but the standard is 4 pages and the maximum 6; shorten the tips and put them on the question; 'remove the deductions and remove the bonus question, but increase the options from 4 to 5, so students get 20 points if they answer totally blindly'; and: how are hand-written answers graded? RULINGS for SEN0401 as a new version v7 (new versioned files only, no gate weakened, no committed file edited): (1) no deductions of any kind: a right answer scores its points, a wrong or blank answer 0, no floor needed, one rule for every question; (2) the bonus question is removed, the total is 100 points; (3) every closed-answer unit has 5 alternatives so a blind guess is worth 1/5: choice 5 options, matching 5 responses per premise, ordering a place from 1 to 5 over 5 steps, fill-in banks of 5 entries; number and code-trace answers stay hand-written (blind chance about 0, so the blind total is slightly under 20: report the exact figure); the fifth option, entry or step is added per item as a new item version, answers unchanged unless a fifth alternative forces otherwise, every key recomputed by running the code; (4) tips: no tips pages; a short tip (target 12 words or fewer) printed on the question itself under the stem; the readability rules (stem 60 words, direction 25 words) stay and its tip rule is updated as a new version; (5) pages: paper plus sheet at most 6, aim 4 or 5 (cover 1, questions 2 to 3, sheet 1); the sheet is one page with choice-type answers only, the reader reads page 1; (6) grading: a plain one-page grading procedure in the instructor key: closed answers by the sheet or the question pages, numbers and traces hand-written on the question page compared with the key value (the exact value gives full points, else 0, no partial credit), the question pages are the legal copy, no arithmetic beyond adding points; (7) cover and directions: every penalty sentence and the two-answers deduction wording removed; the legal-copy sentence and the rule 'two answers in one place count as no answer' stay. The deliverable set carries ONE version: sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_0_0_paper.docx and .pdf, _key.docx and .pdf, _sheet.pdf, and SHA256.txt." .
