ex:CR3_ExamV71 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The exam v7: no deductions, no bonus, five alternatives, short tips, one-page sheet"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:03 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency: 'Design the answer sheet to hold the answers for the question 2. You already provide boxes to fill in.' The owner then answered that the hand-written answers of Question 2 are written ON BOTH the question page and the sheet: the student writes on the question page and copies each into the boxes of the sheet; if they differ the question page counts; the legal-copy rule stays. This makes a new version of the whole set: sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_1_0 (paper, key, sheet, SHA256.txt) as ONE version. Rules: (1) the sheet v7.1 is still ONE A4 page, the same bubbles for the closed answers, plus digit boxes for every hand-written place of Question 2 (2a to 2h as in the structure: numbers and code results), the number of boxes of a place equal to the number of boxes printed on the question page for that place; reuse the number-box design of the v6 sheet module (sen0401_exam_answersheet_v6_1_0.py); the reader v1.4.0 keeps reading bubbles only and treats the boxes as hand-read, and the sheet and the key say so plainly; (2) the printed sentence 5 of the sheet becomes: Write numbers and code results on the question pages and copy each into its boxes here. (at most 25 words); the legal-copy sentences stay and 'Two filled bubbles in one place count as no answer' stays; (3) the paper cover line that says the sheet holds the choice answers only changes to match (the numbers are copied to the sheet, the question pages count); (4) the key 'How to grade': the hand-written step reads the value from the question page, the sheet box is for fast reading; the exact value scores the full points, anything else 0, no partial credit; still one page; (5) pages: paper 5 plus sheet 1 = 6 at most (aim 6 or fewer, measured); the items, the structure and the scoring module are NOT changed (v1.6.1, v1.3.1, v2.0.0). No deduction, no bonus, no floor." .
