    rdfs:label "Backlog widened by the exam v7 stories"@en ;
    backlog:fulfillsRequest ex:CR3_ExamV71 ; backlog:changesScope ex:Scope3 ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:admitsItem ex:ST_Exam_V71_Sheet, ex:ST_Exam_V71_Papers ;
    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:03 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency: 'Design the answer sheet to hold the answers for the question 2. You already provide boxes to fill in.' The owner then answered that the hand-written answers of Question 2 are written ON BOTH the question page and the sheet: the student writes on the question page and copies each into the boxes of the sheet; if they differ the question page counts; the legal-copy rule stays. This makes a new version of the whole set: sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_1_0 (paper, key, sheet, SHA256.txt) as ONE version. Rules: (1) the sheet v7.1 is still ONE A4 page, the same bubbles for the closed answers, plus digit boxes for every hand-written place of Question 2 (2a to 2h as in the structure: numbers and code results), the number of boxes of a place equal to the number of boxes printed on the question page for that place; reuse the number-box design of the v6 sheet module (sen0401_exam_answersheet_v6_1_0.py); the reader v1.4.0 keeps reading bubbles only and treats the boxes as hand-read, and the sheet and the key say so plainly; (2) the printed sentence 5 of the sheet becomes: Write numbers and code results on the question pages and copy each into its boxes here. (at most 25 words); the legal-copy sentences stay and 'Two filled bubbles in one place count as no answer' stays; (3) the paper cover line that says the sheet holds the choice answers only changes to match (the numbers are copied to the sheet, the question pages count); (4) the key 'How to grade': the hand-written step reads the value from the question page, the sheet box is for fast reading; the exact value scores the full points, anything else 0, no partial credit; still one page; (5) pages: paper 5 plus sheet 1 = 6 at most (aim 6 or fewer, measured); the items, the structure and the scoring module are NOT changed (v1.6.1, v1.3.1, v2.0.0). No deduction, no bonus, no floor." .
ex:CR3_ExamV71 rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-11-02 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_ExamV71; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamV71I a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The exam v7: no deductions, no bonus, five alternatives, short tips, one-page sheet"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:06 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency: 'Code questions are crazy. We need to replace them.' The owner then answered: SEN0401 code traces only (SEN0414 stays as delivered); replace them with hand calculations (short number problems from taught material such as fees, halving, hash counts and sizes, answered by a number in the boxes; no code reading). The three Question 2 items whose answer is the output of a program listing are 2a (mt4b:ef1:tries-after-adjustment, critical point CP2.12), 2d (mt2:i11:trace-release-tags, CP3.03) and 2f (mt2:i19:trace-gap-limit, CP5.20), 3, 3 and 4 points. The final set sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_1_0 is rendered on the NEW structure, so the sheet boxes follow the new digit counts. Rules: items v1.7.0 and structure v1.4.0 are NEW files (v1.6.1 and v1.3.1 stay); each replaced item keeps its position, its whole points and holds the same critical point, so no critical point loses its holder (CP3.03 and CP5.20 are held by no other item); taught material only; each answer is a number with an exact value, recomputed by RUNNING code (the calculation is done in code and never shown to students); one Tip of at most 12 words under the stem; stem at most 60 words; NO code listing in any Question 2 item; the R6 repair: the tip of the txid and weight fill-in (4e/4f) is reworded so that SegWit is spelled out at first use (Segregated witness) and the tip keeps at most 12 words; options, answers and points of the other items do not change; no deduction, no bonus, no floor." .
