    rdfs:label "What the exam v7 redesign costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ExamV71I ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:06 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency: 'Code questions are crazy. We need to replace them.' The owner then answered: SEN0401 code traces only (SEN0414 stays as delivered); replace them with hand calculations (short number problems from taught material such as fees, halving, hash counts and sizes, answered by a number in the boxes; no code reading). The three Question 2 items whose answer is the output of a program listing are 2a (mt4b:ef1:tries-after-adjustment, critical point CP2.12), 2d (mt2:i11:trace-release-tags, CP3.03) and 2f (mt2:i19:trace-gap-limit, CP5.20), 3, 3 and 4 points. The final set sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_1_0 is rendered on the NEW structure, so the sheet boxes follow the new digit counts. Rules: items v1.7.0 and structure v1.4.0 are NEW files (v1.6.1 and v1.3.1 stay); each replaced item keeps its position, its whole points and holds the same critical point, so no critical point loses its holder (CP3.03 and CP5.20 are held by no other item); taught material only; each answer is a number with an exact value, recomputed by RUNNING code (the calculation is done in code and never shown to students); one Tip of at most 12 words under the stem; stem at most 60 words; NO code listing in any Question 2 item; the R6 repair: the tip of the txid and weight fill-in (4e/4f) is reworded so that SegWit is spelled out at first use (Segregated witness) and the tip keeps at most 12 words; options, answers and points of the other items do not change; no deduction, no bonus, no floor. AFFECTED: one new story with two tasks (about 4 agent-hours); no existing task depends on it, but every later exam artefact is written to the CME location; the open items are re-ranked (G147)." .
