    backlog:hasScopeChangeRationale "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:06 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency: 'Code questions are crazy. We need to replace them.' The owner then answered: SEN0401 code traces only (SEN0414 stays as delivered); replace them with hand calculations (short number problems from taught material such as fees, halving, hash counts and sizes, answered by a number in the boxes; no code reading). The three Question 2 items whose answer is the output of a program listing are 2a (mt4b:ef1:tries-after-adjustment, critical point CP2.12), 2d (mt2:i11:trace-release-tags, CP3.03) and 2f (mt2:i19:trace-gap-limit, CP5.20), 3, 3 and 4 points. The final set sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_1_0 is rendered on the NEW structure, so the sheet boxes follow the new digit counts. Rules: items v1.7.0 and structure v1.4.0 are NEW files (v1.6.1 and v1.3.1 stay); each replaced item keeps its position, its whole points and holds the same critical point, so no critical point loses its holder (CP3.03 and CP5.20 are held by no other item); taught material only; each answer is a number with an exact value, recomputed by RUNNING code (the calculation is done in code and never shown to students); one Tip of at most 12 words under the stem; stem at most 60 words; NO code listing in any Question 2 item; the R6 repair: the tip of the txid and weight fill-in (4e/4f) is reworded so that SegWit is spelled out at first use (Segregated witness) and the tip keeps at most 12 words; options, answers and points of the other items do not change; no deduction, no bonus, no floor." .
ex:CR3_ExamV71I rdfs:comment "Disposition set to Accepted on 2026-11-02 in the version that records the ScopeChange ex:SC3_ExamV71I; it was Pending before."@en .
ex:CR3_ExamV72 a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "The exam v7: no deductions, no bonus, five alternatives, short tips, one-page sheet"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Scope3 ; backlog:hasChangeDirection backlog:Direction_Grow ; backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted ; rdfs:seeAlso ex:CR3_MidtermSimplify ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:24 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency, deadline: the owner waits to print. Verbatim: 'The questions overall are very hard to understand and rarely human language. Sometimes making references to something not clear at all. Mostly the intention of asking those questions are not well understood. Even the answer key is not enough to solve the question. Too much confusion is added, yet the questions, their intention and answers should be clear and matching. Additionally, the answer sheet shows just the results, no intermediate steps.' Scope: SEN0401 only. The new set is sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_2_0 (paper, key, sheet, SHA256.txt) as ONE version; the sets v7_0_0 (delivered) and v7_1_0 (superseded) stay untouched. ALL 21 items are rewritten for clarity on top of items v1.7.0 and structure v1.4.0 (committed, CME c38bd14; the three code traces already replaced by hand calculations, Q2.c mt7:n2:release-tag-order, Q2.e mt7:n1:target-after-adjustment, Q2.g mt7:n3:keys-checked-by-the-scan); items v1.8.0 and structure v1.5.0 are the new merged files. Requirements: (a) every stem in plain everyday English, one short sentence per idea, no story reference that needs outside context (no unexplained names, dates, block numbers, no 'the story above'), every term the question uses explained in the question itself in one clause, or the question changed to use a term the course defines; (b) one explicit intention sentence as the LAST sentence of the stem, starting 'You are asked to' (for example 'You are asked to choose the statement that is correct.' or 'You are asked to calculate the number of ...'); (c) the options match the intention: each plausible, exactly one right, no trick wording; (d) every item has a plain WORKED SOLUTION for the key: the steps in order with the intermediate numbers for calculations, and for choice, matching, ordering and fill-in items why the right answer is right and, in one clause each, why each other option is wrong; the key renders them (the key is not counted in the 6 pages); (e) a new clarity check (new files) refuses undefined references, a missing intention sentence and a key entry without steps, proven on fixtures of known answer; no existing gate is weakened (R1 stem at most 60 words, R4 format line at most 25 words, tips at most 12 words and R6 abbreviations stay); (f) paper plus sheet at most 6 pages, the sheet one page with the Question 2 boxes; (g) the SegWit tip is spelled out (Segregated witness). The topics, the critical points, the positions, the types and the whole points of the items stay (no critical point loses its holder); the correct answer of an item may change only if the rewrite needs it, and every key value is recomputed by RUNNING code. The student sheet stays results-only by the earlier rulings (exact value, no partial credit); the intermediate steps are in the key. No deduction, no bonus, no floor." .
ex:IA3_ExamV72 a backlog:ImpactAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "What the exam v7 redesign costs and touches"@en ;
    backlog:analyzesRequest ex:CR3_ExamV72 ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage ex:Lineage3 ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "OWNER ORDER (2026-11-02, 21:24 Istanbul, relayed by the coordinator), under the running urgency, deadline: the owner waits to print. Verbatim: 'The questions overall are very hard to understand and rarely human language. Sometimes making references to something not clear at all. Mostly the intention of asking those questions are not well understood. Even the answer key is not enough to solve the question. Too much confusion is added, yet the questions, their intention and answers should be clear and matching. Additionally, the answer sheet shows just the results, no intermediate steps.' Scope: SEN0401 only. The new set is sen0401_exam_midterm_v7_2_0 (paper, key, sheet, SHA256.txt) as ONE version; the sets v7_0_0 (delivered) and v7_1_0 (superseded) stay untouched. ALL 21 items are rewritten for clarity on top of items v1.7.0 and structure v1.4.0 (committed, CME c38bd14; the three code traces already replaced by hand calculations, Q2.c mt7:n2:release-tag-order, Q2.e mt7:n1:target-after-adjustment, Q2.g mt7:n3:keys-checked-by-the-scan); items v1.8.0 and structure v1.5.0 are the new merged files. Requirements: (a) every stem in plain everyday English, one short sentence per idea, no story reference that needs outside context (no unexplained names, dates, block numbers, no 'the story above'), every term the question uses explained in the question itself in one clause, or the question changed to use a term the course defines; (b) one explicit intention sentence as the LAST sentence of the stem, starting 'You are asked to' (for example 'You are asked to choose the statement that is correct.' or 'You are asked to calculate the number of ...'); (c) the options match the intention: each plausible, exactly one right, no trick wording; (d) every item has a plain WORKED SOLUTION for the key: the steps in order with the intermediate numbers for calculations, and for choice, matching, ordering and fill-in items why the right answer is right and, in one clause each, why each other option is wrong; the key renders them (the key is not counted in the 6 pages); (e) a new clarity check (new files) refuses undefined references, a missing intention sentence and a key entry without steps, proven on fixtures of known answer; no existing gate is weakened (R1 stem at most 60 words, R4 format line at most 25 words, tips at most 12 words and R6 abbreviations stay); (f) paper plus sheet at most 6 pages, the sheet one page with the Question 2 boxes; (g) the SegWit tip is spelled out (Segregated witness). The topics, the critical points, the positions, the types and the whole points of the items stay (no critical point loses its holder); the correct answer of an item may change only if the rewrite needs it, and every key value is recomputed by RUNNING code. The student sheet stays results-only by the earlier rulings (exact value, no partial credit); the intermediate steps are in the key. No deduction, no bonus, no floor. AFFECTED: one new story with two tasks (about 4 agent-hours); no existing task depends on it, but every later exam artefact is written to the CME location; the open items are re-ranked (G147)." .
